searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Credentials.Cache","doc":"Long-lived owner of resolved credentials for a repo. Started by the repo\nsupervisor.\n\nThe read path is lock-free: fresh credentials are published to\n`:persistent_term` and `get/1` returns them without touching the process.\nOnly when they are missing or stale does the caller go through the GenServer,\nwhich refreshes once for all concurrent callers (single-flight).","ref":"Dynamo.Credentials.Cache.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Credentials.Cache.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"Dynamo.Credentials.Cache.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Credentials.Cache.get/1","doc":"Returns current (fresh) credentials, refreshing if needed.","ref":"Dynamo.Credentials.Cache.html#get/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Credentials.Cache.invalidate/1","doc":"Drops cached credentials so the next `get/1` re-resolves.","ref":"Dynamo.Credentials.Cache.html#invalidate/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.TypedList","doc":"`{:list, type}` – `L` whose elements are all dumped/loaded with `type`.\nResolved by `Dynamo.Type.resolve!/1`; not used directly.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.TypedList.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.TypedList.dump/2","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.TypedList.html#dump/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.TypedList.load/2","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.TypedList.html#load/2"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Vector","doc":"`:vector` / `{:vector, dimensions}` – a list of floats stored as `L` of `N`,\nthe format DynamoDB vector indexes expect. With a dimension the length is\nchecked on dump and load.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Vector.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Vector.dump/2","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Vector.html#dump/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Vector.load/2","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Vector.html#load/2"},{"type":"task","title":"mix dynamo.create_table","doc":"Creates a DynamoDB table and waits until it is ACTIVE.\n\n    mix dynamo.create_table TABLE_NAME [options]\n    mix dynamo.create_table --schema MyApp.User [options]\n    mix dynamo.create_table --schema MyApp.User --schema MyApp.Order [options]\n\nWith `--schema` the table name, key attribute names and global secondary\nindexes are taken from the schema module. Pass `--schema` several times for a\nsingle-table design: all schemas must share the table and key layout; their\nindexes are merged.","ref":"Mix.Tasks.Dynamo.CreateTable.html"},{"type":"task","title":"Options - mix dynamo.create_table","doc":"--schema           Schema module to derive table/keys/GSIs from (repeatable)\n    --partition-key    Partition key attribute (default: \"pk\")\n    --sort-key         Sort key attribute (default: \"sk\")\n    --no-sort-key      Create a table without a sort key\n    --key-type         Key attribute type S|N|B (default: S)\n    --billing-mode     PAY_PER_REQUEST (default) or PROVISIONED\n    --read-capacity    RCU when PROVISIONED (default: 5)\n    --write-capacity   WCU when PROVISIONED (default: 5)\n    --endpoint         DynamoDB endpoint (e.g. http://localhost:8000)\n    --region           AWS region\n    --repo             Use a started repo's client (e.g. MyApp.Dynamo)\n    --no-wait          Return immediately after CreateTable","ref":"Mix.Tasks.Dynamo.CreateTable.html#module-options"},{"type":"task","title":"mix dynamo.delete_table","doc":"Deletes a DynamoDB table after confirmation.\n\n    mix dynamo.delete_table TABLE_NAME [--force] [--endpoint URL] [--region R] [--repo MyApp.Dynamo]\n\n`--force` skips the prompt. Exits non-zero on failure.","ref":"Mix.Tasks.Dynamo.DeleteTable.html"},{"type":"task","title":"mix dynamo.generate_schema","doc":"Inspects a table (key schema, GSIs and a sample of items) and writes a\nschema module that can read the existing items back.\n\n    mix dynamo.generate_schema TABLE_NAME [options]","ref":"Mix.Tasks.Dynamo.GenerateSchema.html"},{"type":"task","title":"Options - mix dynamo.generate_schema","doc":"--module        Module name (default: derived from the table name)\n    --output        File path (default: lib/ .ex)\n    --scan-items    Items to sample for field discovery (default: 25)\n    --overwrite     Replace an existing file\n    --endpoint / --region / --repo   see other dynamo tasks","ref":"Mix.Tasks.Dynamo.GenerateSchema.html#module-options"},{"type":"task","title":"Key detection - mix dynamo.generate_schema","doc":"If the sampled partition keys look like `entity#value` (this library's\ndefault layout), the generator emits `entity_name` and infers the source\nfield from the sample; otherwise it emits `raw_keys: true` so the key\nattributes are used as-is. Review the generated file – the sample may not\ncover every attribute.","ref":"Mix.Tasks.Dynamo.GenerateSchema.html#module-key-detection"},{"type":"task","title":"mix dynamo.list_tables","doc":"Lists tables, following pagination.\n\n    mix dynamo.list_tables [--name-contains STR] [--endpoint URL] [--region R] [--repo MyApp.Dynamo]","ref":"Mix.Tasks.Dynamo.ListTables.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Page","doc":"A page of results from `query`/`scan`.\n\n  * `:items` – loaded structs\n  * `:last_evaluated_key` – pass as `start_key:` to fetch the next page; `nil` when there is no more data\n  * `:count` – number of items in this page\n  * `:scanned_count` – items examined by DynamoDB before filtering\n  * `:consumed_capacity` – present when `return_consumed_capacity:` was requested\n\n`Dynamo.Page` implements `Enumerable`, so you can `Enum.map(page, ...)` directly.","ref":"Dynamo.Page.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Page.more?/1","doc":"True when another page can be fetched.","ref":"Dynamo.Page.html#more?/1"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Page.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Page.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Dynamo.Repo","doc":"Defines a repository: a supervised process tree that owns the DynamoDB client\n(region, endpoint, credentials, retry policy) and exposes the operations.\n\n    defmodule MyApp.Dynamo do\n      use Dynamo.Repo, otp_app: :my_app\n    end\n\n    # config/runtime.exs\n    config :my_app, MyApp.Dynamo,\n      region: System.get_env(\"AWS_REGION\", \"eu-central-1\"),\n      endpoint: System.get_env(\"DYNAMO_ENDPOINT\")   # e.g. http://localhost:8000 for DynamoDB Local\n\n    # application.ex\n    children = [MyApp.Dynamo]","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Configuration - Dynamo.Repo","doc":"Read from `Application.get_env(otp_app, MyRepo)` and overridable via\n`init/1`:\n\n  * `:region` (required unless `:endpoint` is given – then defaults to `\"us-east-1\"`)\n  * `:endpoint` – custom URL (DynamoDB Local, VPC endpoint)\n  * `:search_endpoint` – URL for `SearchVectors` (default `https://search-dynamodb. .amazonaws.com`)\n  * `:access_key_id`, `:secret_access_key`, `:session_token` – static credentials\n    (otherwise env → ECS → IMDS, see `Dynamo.Credentials`)\n  * `:max_retries`, `:base_backoff_ms`, `:max_backoff_ms`, `:receive_timeout`,\n    `:connect_timeout`, `:req_options`, `:telemetry_prefix` – see `Dynamo.Client`\n  * `:batch_retries` – how many times unprocessed batch items are retried (default 5)","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Operations - Dynamo.Repo","doc":"Every function returns `{:ok, result} | {:error, %Dynamo.Error{}}` and has a\nbang variant that raises the error.\n\n  * `put/2`, `get/2`, `delete/2`, `update/3`\n  * `query/2`, `scan/2` → `%Dynamo.Page{}`; `query_all/2`, `scan_all/2` →\n    list (bounded by `:limit`); `stream/2` (see `Dynamo.Stream`)\n  * `batch_write/2`, `batch_get/2` – automatically chunked and unprocessed\n    items retried with backoff\n  * `transaction/2` – `TransactWriteItems`\n  * `search_vectors/4` – `SearchVectors` on a `vector_index`\n  * `request/2` – raw action escape hatch\n\nOptions are documented on `Dynamo.Request`.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#module-operations"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.batch_get/3","doc":"BatchGetItem for any number of structs of one schema. Chunks into 100,\nretries `UnprocessedKeys`. Returns `{:ok, %{items: [struct], unprocessed_keys: [key_map]}}`.\nItems are returned in arbitrary order (DynamoDB does not preserve order).","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#batch_get/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.batch_write/3","doc":"BatchWriteItem for any number of structs / `{:delete, struct}` tuples.\nChunks into 25, retries `UnprocessedItems` with backoff up to\n`:batch_retries` times. Returns `{:ok, %{unprocessed: [raw_requests]}}` –\n`unprocessed` is empty on full success. Any non-retryable error aborts and\nis returned.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#batch_write/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.delete/3","doc":"DeleteItem. `{:ok, nil}` or, with `return_values: :all_old`, `{:ok, old_struct | nil}`.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#delete/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.get/3","doc":"GetItem. `{:ok, struct}` or `{:ok, nil}` when not found.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#get/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Dynamo.Repo.init/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#c:init/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.put/3","doc":"PutItem. Returns the struct; with `return_values: :all_old` returns the previous item (or nil).","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#put/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.query/3","doc":"Query one page.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#query/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.query_all/3","doc":"Query all pages into a list. `:limit` bounds the total number of items\nreturned (pages are requested until that many items are collected or the\ndata is exhausted). Without `:limit` this loads the whole partition.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#query_all/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.request/3","doc":"Raw escape hatch.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#request/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.scan/3","doc":"Scan one page.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#scan/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.scan_all/3","doc":"Scan all pages into a list (bounded by `:limit`). Expensive – prefer `stream/2`.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#scan_all/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.search_vectors/5","doc":"Vector similarity search on a schema's `vector_index`. Returns the top-k\nitems as `{struct, score}` pairs, most similar first. Score semantics follow\nthe index distance function: lower is closer for `:cosine`/`:euclidean`,\nhigher for `:dot_product`.\n\n    {:ok, %{results: [{%Doc{} = doc, 0.12}, ...], consumed_capacity: cc}} =\n      MyRepo.search_vectors(Doc, \"Semantic\", embedding, top_k: 5, filter: [lang: \"en\"])\n\nThe vector index is eventually consistent; a freshly written item may not be\nfound immediately. Projection determines which fields are populated on the\nreturned structs (others keep their defaults).","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#search_vectors/5"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.transaction/3","doc":"TransactWriteItems. See `Dynamo.Request.transact_write/2` for operation shapes.\nOn cancellation the returned error has `type: :transaction_canceled` and\n`cancellation_reasons` (one per operation, in order).","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#transaction/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Repo.update/4","doc":"UpdateItem. Returns `{:ok, nil}` unless `return_values:` asks for attributes.","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#update/4"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Repo.result/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Repo.html#t:result/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Stream","doc":"Lazy streams over paginated `Query`/`Scan` results.\n\n    # all orders of a user, lazily page by page\n    MyApp.Dynamo.stream(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"})\n    |> Stream.filter(&(&1.status == \"open\"))\n    |> Enum.take(100)\n\n    # whole-table scan\n    MyApp.Dynamo.stream(User, filter: \"attribute_exists(#e)\", names: %{\"#e\" => \"email\"})\n    |> Enum.each(&process/1)\n\n    # truly parallel scan: N segments fetched concurrently, results interleaved\n    MyApp.Dynamo.stream(User, segments: 8, max_concurrency: 4)\n    |> Enum.count()\n\nPass a **struct** to query (partition key from the struct, see\n`Dynamo.Request.query/2`) or a **schema module** to scan.\n\nOptions: all `Dynamo.Request` query/scan options, plus\n\n  * `:page_size` – maps to DynamoDB `Limit` per request (default: unset)\n  * `:segments` – scan only; number of parallel segments (default 1)\n  * `:max_concurrency` – scan only; concurrent segment fetches (default `segments`)\n\nErrors raise `%Dynamo.Error{}` while the stream is consumed (the only way to\nsignal failure from inside a stream). Scans consume read capacity for every\nitem examined – stream lazily, but do not stream casually.","ref":"Dynamo.Stream.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Stream.new/3","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Stream.html#new/3"},{"type":"protocol","title":"Dynamo.Encodable","doc":"Protocol used by the `:any` type (and nested `:map`/`:list` values) to encode\nstructs and custom values that have no explicit field type.\n\nPrefer an explicit `Dynamo.Type` on the schema field. Implement this protocol\nfor values you want to embed inside `:map`/`:list`/`:any` fields:\n\n    defimpl Dynamo.Encodable, for: Money do\n      def dump(m), do: {:ok, %{\"N\" => Money.to_string(m)}}\n    end\n\nSchemas defined with `Dynamo.Schema` get an implementation automatically that\ndumps them as a nested `M`.\n\nDecoding is one-directional: nested structs are loaded as plain string-keyed\nmaps. Use a `Dynamo.Type` if you need typed nested structs.","ref":"Dynamo.Encodable.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Encodable.dump/1","doc":"Returns `{:ok, attribute_value}` or `:error`.","ref":"Dynamo.Encodable.html#dump/1"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Encodable.t/0","doc":"All the types that implement this protocol.","ref":"Dynamo.Encodable.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Key","doc":"A resolved DynamoDB primary key for a table or index.\n\nProduced by `Dynamo.Schema.primary_key/1` and `Dynamo.Schema.index_key/2`;\nconsumed by `Dynamo.Request`. `pk`/`sk` are DynamoDB attribute values\n(`%{\"S\" => ...}`), `pk_name`/`sk_name` the attribute names.","ref":"Dynamo.Key.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Key.to_map/1","doc":"Renders the key as a DynamoDB `Key` map.","ref":"Dynamo.Key.html#to_map/1"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Key.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Key.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Raw","doc":"Wraps a value that is *already* in DynamoDB attribute-value format so the\nencoder passes it through untouched.\n\n    %Dynamo.Raw{value: %{\"B\" => Base.encode64(bytes)}}\n\nThis is the only way to inject pre-encoded values; plain maps that happen to\nhave keys like `\"S\"` or `\"N\"` are always treated as user data.","ref":"Dynamo.Raw.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Raw.new/1","doc":"Wraps an attribute value, validating that it has exactly one known type tag.","ref":"Dynamo.Raw.html#new/1"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Raw.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Raw.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Schema","doc":"Defines a DynamoDB item schema with typed fields, keys and indexes.\n\n    defmodule MyApp.Order do\n      use Dynamo.Schema\n\n      item do\n        table \"app_data\"\n        entity_name \"order\"            # prefix used in generated keys (default: module basename)\n\n        field :user_id, :string, partition_key: true\n        field :placed_at, :utc_datetime, sort_key: true\n        field :order_id, :string, sort_key: true\n        field :total, :decimal\n        field :status, :string, default: \"pending\"\n        field :tags, :string_set\n\n        global_secondary_index \"StatusIndex\", partition_key: :status, sort_key: :placed_at\n      end\n    end","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Fields - Dynamo.Schema","doc":"`field name, type \\\\ :string, opts`. Types are the built-ins listed in\n`Dynamo.Type` or a module implementing `Dynamo.Type`. Options:\n\n  * `:default` – struct default\n  * `:partition_key` / `:sort_key` – include this field in the composite key\n    (in declaration order); alternatively use `partition_key [...]` /\n    `sort_key [...]`.\n  * `:required` – `dump/1` returns an error when the value is `nil`","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#module-fields"},{"type":"module","title":"Key generation - Dynamo.Schema","doc":"The table's partition/sort key attributes are named by the `partition_key_name`\n/ `sort_key_name` options (default `\"pk\"` / `\"sk\"`). Their *values* are built by\njoining the dumped, stringified key field values with `key_separator` (default\n`\"#\"`):\n\n    pk = \"     …\"\n    sk = \"   …\"             (with `prefix_sort_key: true`: \"    …\")\n\nEvery partition-key field must be non-nil – a nil produces a\n`{:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :validation_error}}`. Sort-key fields may be\n*partially* populated: generation stops at the first `nil`, which yields a\nprefix usable with `begins_with` queries. Separator characters inside key\nvalues are rejected so keys always round-trip.\n\nSet `raw_keys: true` to use the first partition/sort key field *as is*\n(no entity prefix, no joining) – for tables not designed around this\nlibrary. In that mode the key attribute names default to the field names.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#module-key-generation"},{"type":"module","title":"Options (to `use Dynamo.Schema`) - Dynamo.Schema","doc":"* `:partition_key_name`, `:sort_key_name` – attribute names (default \"pk\"/\"sk\")\n  * `:key_separator` – default \"#\"\n  * `:prefix_sort_key` – default false\n  * `:raw_keys` – default false\n  * `:omit_nil` – omit nil fields from written items (default true)","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#module-options-to-use-dynamo-schema"},{"type":"module","title":"Embedded schemas - Dynamo.Schema","doc":"A schema module can be used as a field type. Declare it with\n`use Dynamo.Schema, embedded: true` (no table, keys or indexes) and nest it\ndirectly or inside a typed list:\n\n    defmodule MyApp.Address do\n      use Dynamo.Schema, embedded: true\n      item do\n        field :street, :string\n        field :city, :string\n        field :geo, {:list, :float}\n      end\n    end\n\n    field :address, MyApp.Address\n    field :previous_addresses, {:list, MyApp.Address}\n\nEmbedded values round-trip with full typing (dates stay dates, decimals stay\ndecimals). Any table schema can also be embedded; its key attributes are not\nincluded when nested.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#module-embedded-schemas"},{"type":"module","title":"Generated functions - Dynamo.Schema","doc":"`__schema__/1` (`:table`, `:fields`, `:field_types`, `:partition_key`,\n`:sort_key`, `:indexes`, `:vector_indexes`, `:options`, `:entity_name`),\n`__schema__/2` (`{:type, field}`, `{:index, name}`, `{:vector_index, name}`).","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#module-generated-functions"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.assert_schema!/1","doc":"Raises unless `module` is a schema.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#assert_schema!/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.dump/1","doc":"Dumps a struct into a DynamoDB item map, including the generated key\nattributes. Nil fields are omitted when `omit_nil` is true.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.dump!/1","doc":"Like `dump/1` but raises.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#dump!/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.dump_attributes/1","doc":"Dumps only the declared fields (no generated key attributes).","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#dump_attributes/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.entity_name/1","doc":"Sets the entity prefix used in generated partition keys.\n\nAccepts a string, or another `Dynamo.Schema` module whose entity name is\ninherited at compile time. Use the module form to place child items in a\nparent's partition without duplicating the string:\n\n    defmodule Shop.Order do\n      use Dynamo.Schema\n      item do\n        table \"shop\"\n        entity_name Shop.Customer                            # pk = \"customer# \"\n        field :customer_id, :string, partition_key: true\n        field :kind, :string, sort_key: true, default: \"order\"\n        field :order_id, :string, sort_key: true\n      end\n    end\n\nRenaming `Shop.Customer` then moves both entities together; a typo is a\ncompile error instead of a silently different partition.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#entity_name/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.field/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#field/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.field/2","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#field/2"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.field/3","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#field/3"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.global_secondary_index/2","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#global_secondary_index/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.index_key/2","doc":"Resolves the key for a global secondary index. The GSI partition key field\nmust be non-nil; the sort key is nil when unpopulated. Values are dumped with\ntheir field types (so numeric GSI keys stay `N`).","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#index_key/2"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.item/1","doc":"Defines the item. Must contain exactly one `table` and at least one partition key field.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#item/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.key_names/1","doc":"Returns the `{partition_key_name, sort_key_name}` attribute names for the\nschema's table. `sort_key_name` is nil when the schema has no sort key.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#key_names/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.load/2","doc":"Loads a DynamoDB item map into a struct. Unknown attributes (including the\ngenerated key attributes) are ignored. Returns `{:error, %Dynamo.Error{}}`\nwhen a value cannot be loaded with the field's type.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#load/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.load!/2","doc":"Like `load/2` but raises.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#load!/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.load_all/2","doc":"Loads a list of items, stopping at the first error.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#load_all/2"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.partition_key/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#partition_key/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.partition_key_value/1","doc":"Computes the partition key attribute value for a struct.\nAll partition key fields must be non-nil.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#partition_key_value/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.primary_key/1","doc":"Resolves the table primary key for a struct.\n\nReturns `{:ok, %Dynamo.Key{}}` or `{:error, %Dynamo.Error{}}` when a\npartition key field is nil or a key value contains the separator.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#primary_key/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.primary_key!/1","doc":"Like `primary_key/1` but raises.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#primary_key!/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.schema?/1","doc":"Returns true if `module` was defined with `Dynamo.Schema`.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#schema?/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.sort_key/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#sort_key/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Schema.sort_key_value/1","doc":"Computes the sort key attribute value for a struct, or `{:ok, nil}` when the\nschema has no sort key or no sort key field is populated. Stops at the first\nnil field (partial sort key).","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#sort_key_value/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.table/1","doc":"Sets the table name. Accepts a literal or any expression evaluated at compile\ntime, e.g. `table Application.compile_env!(:my_app, :orders_table)` or\n`table \"orders_\" <> System.get_env(\"ENV\", \"dev\")`.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#table/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Dynamo.Schema.vector_index/2","doc":"Declares a DynamoDB vector index over a `:vector` field.\n\n    field :embedding, {:vector, 1024}\n    field :tenant, :string\n    field :lang, :string\n\n    vector_index \"Semantic\",\n      field: :embedding,\n      distance: :cosine,                   # :cosine | :dot_product | :euclidean\n      projection: :include, projected_attributes: [:title],\n      partition_key: :tenant,              # optional; searches must then pass it\n      filters: [:lang]                     # optional inline filter attributes\n\n`dimensions:` defaults to the field's `{:vector, n}` size. Search with\n`Dynamo.Repo.search_vectors/4`. Vector indexes require on-demand billing.","ref":"Dynamo.Schema.html#vector_index/2"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Dynamo.Type","doc":"Behaviour for schema field types.\n\nA type converts between an Elixir value and a DynamoDB *attribute value*\n(`%{\"S\" => \"...\"}`, `%{\"N\" => \"1\"}`, …).\n\n    defmodule MyApp.Type.Money do\n      use Dynamo.Type\n\n      def dump(%Money{} = m), do: {:ok, %{\"N\" => Money.to_string(m)}}\n      def dump(_), do: :error\n\n      def load(%{\"N\" => n}), do: {:ok, Money.parse!(n)}\n      def load(_), do: :error\n    end\n\n    field :price, MyApp.Type.Money","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Built-in types - Dynamo.Type","doc":"| Atom               | Elixir value              | DynamoDB |\n|--------------------|---------------------------|----------|\n| `:string`          | `String.t()`              | `S`      |\n| `:integer`         | `integer()`               | `N`      |\n| `:float`           | `float()`                 | `N`      |\n| `:decimal`         | `Decimal.t()` (optional dep) | `N`   |\n| `:boolean`         | `boolean()`               | `BOOL`   |\n| `:binary`          | `binary()`                | `B`      |\n| `:utc_datetime`    | `DateTime.t()` (ISO 8601) | `S`      |\n| `:naive_datetime`  | `NaiveDateTime.t()`       | `S`      |\n| `:date`            | `Date.t()`                | `S`      |\n| `:time`            | `Time.t()`                | `S`      |\n| `:map`             | `map()` (string keys)     | `M`      |\n| `:list`            | `list()`                  | `L`      |\n| `:string_set`      | `MapSet.t(String.t())`    | `SS`     |\n| `:number_set`      | `MapSet.t(number())`      | `NS`     |\n| `:binary_set`      | `MapSet.t(binary())`      | `BS`     |\n| `:any`             | inferred via `Dynamo.Encodable` | any |\n| `{:list, type}`    | `[type]`                  | `L`      |\n| `:vector`, `{:vector, n}` | `[float()]` (embedding) | `L` of `N` |\n| a `Dynamo.Schema`  | that struct (embedded)    | `M`      |\n\n`nil` is handled uniformly: it dumps to `%{\"NULL\" => true}` and loads back to\n`nil` for every type. Fields that are `nil` are omitted from written items by\ndefault (see `Dynamo.Schema`).","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#module-built-in-types"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.builtin/0","doc":"Returns the list of built-in type atoms.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#builtin/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"Dynamo.Type.cast/1","doc":"Casts loosely typed input (e.g. from params) into the Elixir value. Optional.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#c:cast/1"},{"type":"callback","title":"Dynamo.Type.dump/1","doc":"Converts an Elixir value into a DynamoDB attribute value.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#c:dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.dump/2","doc":"Dumps a value with the given type. `nil` always becomes `NULL`.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#dump/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.dump!/3","doc":"Dumps a value or raises `ArgumentError` with an actionable message.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#dump!/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Dynamo.Type.load/1","doc":"Converts a DynamoDB attribute value back into an Elixir value.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#c:load/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.load/2","doc":"Loads a DynamoDB attribute value with the given type. `NULL` always becomes `nil`.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#load/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.load!/3","doc":"Loads or raises.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#load!/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.resolve!/1","doc":"Resolves a type spec (builtin atom or module) to a module implementing\n`Dynamo.Type`. Raises `ArgumentError` for unknown types.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#resolve!/1"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Type.dynamo_value/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.html#t:dynamo_value/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Condition","doc":"Builds `ConditionExpression` / `FilterExpression` strings from Elixir terms,\ngenerating attribute-name and value placeholders so you never write\n`names:`/`values:` by hand.\n\nAny `condition:` or `filter:` option accepts either a raw string (with your\nown `names:`/`values:`) or one of these forms:\n\n    # keyword list = AND of field conditions\n    condition: [status: \"open\", version: {:eq, 3}]\n    condition: [age: {:gt, 18}, tags: {:contains, \"vip\"}, name: {:begins_with, \"A\"}]\n    condition: [price: {:between, 10, 20}, kind: {:in, [\"a\", \"b\"]}]\n    condition: [email: :exists, legacy: :not_exists]\n    condition: [total: {:size, {:gt, 3}}, meta: {:attribute_type, \"M\"}]\n\n    # combinators\n    condition: {:or, [status: \"open\"], [status: \"pending\"]}\n    condition: {:and, [a: 1], {:not, [b: 2]}}\n\nField operators: a plain value means `=`; `{:eq | :ne | :lt | :lte | :gt | :gte, v}`,\n`{:between, lo, hi}`, `{:in, [v, ...]}`, `{:begins_with, s}`, `{:contains, v}`,\n`:exists` / `:not_exists`, `{:attribute_type, \"S\" | \"N\" | ...}`,\n`{:size, {op, n}}`.\n\nFields may be atoms, strings, or nested paths as lists (`[:address, :city]`\n→ `#a0.#a1`). Values are dumped with the schema's field type for top-level\nfields when a schema is given, otherwise inferred (`:any`).\n\nPlaceholders are `#c0…` and `:c0…` so they never collide with the `#a0`/`:v0`\nplaceholders from `Dynamo.Update` or `:pk`/`:sk` from key conditions.","ref":"Dynamo.Condition.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Condition.build/3","doc":"Compiles a condition. Strings pass through untouched (names/values empty).\nReturns `{:ok, expression, names, values}`.","ref":"Dynamo.Condition.html#build/3"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Condition.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Condition.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Update","doc":"Builds DynamoDB `UpdateExpression`s from a keyword list or map of changes.\n\nUsed by `Dynamo.Repo.update/3` and `Dynamo.Repo.transaction/2`. Values are\ndumped with the schema's field type when a schema is given, otherwise with\n`:any`.\n\n    Dynamo.Update.build(User, name: \"Jane\", login_count: {:increment, 1}, legacy: :remove)\n    #=> {:ok, %{\n    #     \"UpdateExpression\" => \"SET #a0 = :v0, #a1 = #a1 + :v1 REMOVE #a2\",\n    #     \"ExpressionAttributeNames\" => %{\"#a0\" => \"name\", \"#a1\" => \"login_count\", \"#a2\" => \"legacy\"},\n    #     \"ExpressionAttributeValues\" => %{\":v0\" => %{\"S\" => \"Jane\"}, \":v1\" => %{\"N\" => \"1\"}}\n    #   }}","ref":"Dynamo.Update.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Operators - Dynamo.Update","doc":"* `value` – `SET field = value`\n  * `{:increment, n}` / `{:decrement, n}` – `SET field = field + n` (field must exist)\n  * `{:add, n}` – `ADD field n` (atomic counter; creates the attribute if missing)\n  * `{:add, set}` – `ADD field set` (adds elements to a set)\n  * `{:delete, set}` – `DELETE field set` (removes elements from a set)\n  * `{:append, list}` / `{:prepend, list}` – `SET field = list_append(...)`\n  * `{:if_not_exists, value}` – `SET field = if_not_exists(field, value)`\n  * `:remove` – `REMOVE field`\n\nPlaceholders are generated (`#a0`, `:v0`…) so attribute names never need to be\nvalid identifiers and reserved words are always safe.","ref":"Dynamo.Update.html#module-operators"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Update.build/2","doc":"Builds the expression parts. `schema` may be `nil` (values dumped as `:any`).\nKey fields of the schema are rejected — updating a key requires delete + put.","ref":"Dynamo.Update.html#build/2"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Update.change/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Update.html#t:change/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Update.result/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Update.html#t:result/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Request","doc":"Pure builders for DynamoDB request payloads.\n\nEvery function returns `{:ok, {action, payload}}` or `{:error, %Dynamo.Error{}}`\nand performs **no I/O**. `Dynamo.Repo` executes them through `Dynamo.Client`.\nBecause they are pure they can be unit-tested against the exact JSON DynamoDB\nexpects.","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Common options - Dynamo.Request","doc":"Most builders accept these expression options:\n\n  * `:condition` – `ConditionExpression` string\n  * `:filter` – `FilterExpression` string (query/scan)\n  * `:projection` – `ProjectionExpression` string or list of field atoms\n  * `:names` – map of `\"#placeholder\" => \"attribute\"` (`ExpressionAttributeNames`)\n  * `:values` – map of `\":placeholder\" => value`. Values that are not already\n    DynamoDB attribute values (`Dynamo.Raw`) are dumped with `:any`.\n  * `:return_values` – `:none | :all_old | :all_new | :updated_old | :updated_new`\n  * `:return_consumed_capacity` – `:none | :total | :indexes`","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#module-common-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.batch_get/2","doc":"BatchGetItem for up to 100 structs (same schema).","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#batch_get/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.batch_write/2","doc":"BatchWriteItem for up to 25 structs (mixed schemas/tables allowed).\n`{:delete, struct}` tuples delete instead of put.","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#batch_write/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.delete/2","doc":"DeleteItem.","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#delete/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.get/2","doc":"GetItem for a schema struct with populated key fields.","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#get/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.put/2","doc":"PutItem for a schema struct.","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#put/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.query/2","doc":"Query. The partition key is taken from the struct (table or `:index`). The\nsort key condition comes from `:sort_key`:\n\n  * omitted – if the struct has sort-key fields populated: `begins_with` on the\n    generated (possibly partial) composite sort key for table queries, or\n    equality for index / `raw_keys` queries (single typed attribute);\n    otherwise partition only\n  * `{:eq, v}`, `{:lt, v}`, `{:lte, v}`, `{:gt, v}`, `{:gte, v}`,\n    `{:begins_with, v}`, `{:between, lo, hi}` – explicit condition; `v` is the\n    raw sort key value (string for composite keys, typed value for GSI/raw keys)\n  * `:none` – partition key only, ignore struct sort-key fields\n\nOther options: `:filter`, `:projection`, `:names`, `:values`, `:limit`,\n`:start_key`, `:consistent` (not allowed with `:index`), `:descending`,\n`:select` (`:count`, `:all_attributes`, `:all_projected_attributes`).","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#query/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.scan/2","doc":"Scan a schema's table (or `:index`). Supports `:segment`/`:total_segments`.","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#scan/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.search_vectors/4","doc":"SearchVectors on a schema's vector index.\n\n  * `vector` – list of floats; its length must match the index dimensions\n  * `:top_k` – 1..100 (default 10)\n  * `:filter` – `SearchConditionExpression`; string or `Dynamo.Condition` DSL.\n    When the index has a `partition_key`, the filter MUST include\n    `[partition_field: value]` (DynamoDB requires it).\n  * `:projection` – attributes to return (only projected ones are available);\n    the vector itself is not returned unless you ask for it here\n  * `:return_consumed_capacity` – `:total | :indexes | :none`","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#search_vectors/4"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.transact_write/2","doc":"TransactWriteItems. Each operation is one of:\n\n  * `{:put, struct, opts}` – `opts`: `:condition`, `:names`, `:values`\n  * `{:update, struct, changes, opts}`\n  * `{:delete, struct, opts}`\n  * `{:check, struct, condition, opts}` – `ConditionCheck`\n\n(`opts` may be omitted.) Top-level `opts`: `:client_request_token` for\nidempotency, `:return_consumed_capacity`.","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#transact_write/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Request.update/3","doc":"UpdateItem. `changes` is a keyword/map of `field => change` (see\n`Dynamo.Update`), or pass `update_expression:` with `names:`/`values:` for a\nraw expression.","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#update/3"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Request.action/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#t:action/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Request.payload/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#t:payload/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Request.result/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Request.html#t:result/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Client","doc":"Low-level DynamoDB HTTP client: SigV4 signing, retries with jittered\nexponential backoff, error normalisation and telemetry.\n\nYou normally don't call this directly – `Dynamo.Repo` does. It is exposed\nfor tooling (mix tasks) and for people who want to send raw requests.\n\n    client = Dynamo.Client.new(region: \"eu-west-1\", credentials: creds)\n    Dynamo.Client.request(client, \"ListTables\", %{})\n    #=> {:ok, %{\"TableNames\" => [...]}}","ref":"Dynamo.Client.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Options - Dynamo.Client","doc":"* `:region` – required\n  * `:endpoint` – full URL; defaults to `https://dynamodb. .amazonaws.com`\n  * `:search_endpoint` – endpoint for `SearchVectors`, which AWS serves from a\n    separate host; defaults to `https://search-dynamodb. .amazonaws.com`.\n    When a custom `:endpoint` is given (DynamoDB Local, a proxy), it is used for\n    search too unless `:search_endpoint` is set explicitly.\n  * `:credentials` – `%Dynamo.Credentials{}` or `{:cache, pid_or_name}` of a\n    `Dynamo.Credentials.Cache` (used by repos so credentials refresh automatically)\n  * `:max_retries` – default 3 (only retryable errors are retried)\n  * `:base_backoff_ms` – default 50; delay = random(0, base * 2^attempt) capped at `:max_backoff_ms` (default 5_000)\n  * `:receive_timeout` – default 30_000\n  * `:connect_timeout` – default 5_000\n  * `:req_options` – extra options merged into every `Req` call (e.g. `plug:` for tests)\n  * `:telemetry_prefix` – default `[:dynamo]`","ref":"Dynamo.Client.html#module-options"},{"type":"module","title":"Telemetry - Dynamo.Client","doc":"`[prefix, :request, :start | :stop | :exception]` with measurements\n`%{duration: native}` on stop and metadata:\n\n    %{action: \"Query\", table: \"app\" | nil, attempt: 1, result: :ok | :error,\n      error: %Dynamo.Error{} | nil, status: 200, consumed_capacity: map | nil}","ref":"Dynamo.Client.html#module-telemetry"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Client.new/1","doc":"Builds a client. Raises on missing `:region` or `:credentials`.","ref":"Dynamo.Client.html#new/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Client.request/3","doc":"Sends a DynamoDB action. Returns the decoded JSON body or a normalised error.","ref":"Dynamo.Client.html#request/3"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Client.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Client.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Credentials","doc":"AWS credential resolution.\n\nResolution order (first match wins):\n\n1. Static credentials passed in repo config (`access_key_id` / `secret_access_key` / `session_token`)\n2. Environment: `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN`\n3. ECS/Fargate container credentials (`AWS_CONTAINER_CREDENTIALS_FULL_URI` or `_RELATIVE_URI`)\n4. EC2 instance metadata (IMDSv2)\n\nCredentials from metadata endpoints carry an expiry; `Dynamo.Credentials.Cache`\n(owned by the repo supervisor) refreshes them a few minutes before they expire\nand guarantees only one refresh happens at a time.","ref":"Dynamo.Credentials.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Credentials.resolve/1","doc":"Resolve credentials once, without caching.\n\nOptions: `:access_key_id`/`:secret_access_key`/`:session_token` (static),\n`:disable_imds`, `:req_options` (merged into metadata HTTP calls – e.g. a\n`plug:` in tests), and for tests `:env` (map used instead of `System.get_env/1`),\n`:ecs_host`, `:imds_base`.","ref":"Dynamo.Credentials.html#resolve/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Credentials.stale?/1","doc":"True when the credentials need refreshing (expiry within the buffer).","ref":"Dynamo.Credentials.html#stale?/1"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Credentials.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Credentials.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"exception","title":"Dynamo.Error","doc":"The single error type returned by every Dynamo operation.\n\nAll failures — AWS service errors, transport errors and local validation\nfailures — are normalised into `%Dynamo.Error{}` at the client boundary, so\ncode above the client never has to inspect raw AWS payloads.\n\n    case MyApp.Repo.put(user, condition: \"attribute_not_exists(pk)\") do\n      {:ok, user} -> ...\n      {:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :conditional_check_failed}} -> ...\n      {:error, %Dynamo.Error{retryable?: true} = e} -> retry_later(e)\n    end","ref":"Dynamo.Error.html"},{"type":"exception","title":"Fields - Dynamo.Error","doc":"* `:type` – categorised atom, e.g. `:resource_not_found`,\n    `:conditional_check_failed`, `:throttled`, `:validation_error`,\n    `:transaction_canceled`, `:transport_error`\n  * `:message` – human readable message\n  * `:aws_type` – the un-namespaced AWS exception name, when applicable\n  * `:status` – HTTP status, when applicable\n  * `:retryable?` – whether retrying the same request may succeed\n  * `:cancellation_reasons` – for `:transaction_canceled`, one entry per\n    transact item with `code`, `message` and `item`\n  * `:details` – any additional structured data (raw AWS body, exception…)","ref":"Dynamo.Error.html#module-fields"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Error.from_aws/2","doc":"Normalises an AWS error response body (already JSON decoded) plus HTTP status.\n\nHandles both `\"__type\"` forms DynamoDB uses (`\"ResourceNotFoundException\"`\nand `\"com.amazonaws.dynamodb.v20120810#ResourceNotFoundException\"`) and both\nmessage keys (`\"message\"` and `\"Message\"`).","ref":"Dynamo.Error.html#from_aws/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Error.new/3","doc":"Builds a local (non-AWS) error, e.g. a validation failure.","ref":"Dynamo.Error.html#new/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Error.retryable?/1","doc":"Whether an error of this type is worth retrying.","ref":"Dynamo.Error.html#retryable?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Error.transport/1","doc":"Wraps a transport level failure (connection refused, timeout…).","ref":"Dynamo.Error.html#transport/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Error.validation/2","doc":"Builds a `:validation_error`.","ref":"Dynamo.Error.html#validation/2"},{"type":"type","title":"Dynamo.Error.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Error.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Any","doc":"`:any` – type inferred from the Elixir value on dump and from the DynamoDB\ntag on load. Uses the `Dynamo.Encodable` protocol for structs and custom\nvalues. Use an explicit type when you can; `:any` cannot round-trip atoms,\ndates or decimals, and always loads numbers as integers/floats.\n\nInference rules on dump: binaries → `S` (never `B` – use `Dynamo.Raw` or\n`:binary`), integers/floats → `N`, booleans → `BOOL`, `nil` → `NULL`,\nlists → `L`, maps → `M`, `MapSet` → `SS`/`NS` by element type, structs →\n`Dynamo.Encodable`.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Any.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Any.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Any.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Any.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Any.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Any.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Any.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Binary","doc":"`:binary` – `B` (base64 on the wire). Never inferred; always explicit.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Binary.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Binary.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Binary.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Binary.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Binary.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Binary.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Binary.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.BinarySet","doc":"`:binary_set` – `BS` (base64 on the wire). Empty sets dump to `NULL`.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.BinarySet.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.BinarySet.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.BinarySet.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.BinarySet.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.BinarySet.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.BinarySet.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.BinarySet.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Boolean","doc":"`:boolean` – `BOOL`.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Boolean.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Boolean.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Boolean.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Boolean.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Boolean.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Boolean.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Boolean.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Date","doc":"`:date` – `S` ISO 8601 date.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Date.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Date.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Date.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Date.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Date.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Date.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Date.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Decimal","doc":"`:decimal` – `N`, using the optional `decimal` dependency for exact\narbitrary-precision numbers (the correct choice for money).","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Decimal.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Decimal.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Decimal.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Decimal.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Decimal.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Decimal.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Decimal.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Float","doc":"`:float` – `N`. Integers are accepted on dump.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Float.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Float.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Float.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Float.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Float.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Float.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Float.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Integer","doc":"`:integer` – `N`.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Integer.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Integer.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Integer.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Integer.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Integer.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Integer.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Integer.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.List","doc":"`:list` – `L`. Elements are encoded with `Dynamo.Type.Any`.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.List.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.List.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.List.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.List.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.List.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.List.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.List.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Map","doc":"`:map` – `M`. Values are encoded with `Dynamo.Type.Any` (inferred). Keys are\nconverted to strings on dump and stay strings on load.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Map.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Map.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Map.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Map.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Map.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Map.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Map.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.NaiveDateTime","doc":"`:naive_datetime` – `S` ISO 8601 without offset.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.NaiveDateTime.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.NaiveDateTime.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.NaiveDateTime.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.NaiveDateTime.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.NaiveDateTime.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.NaiveDateTime.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.NaiveDateTime.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.NumberSet","doc":"`:number_set` – `NS`. Empty sets dump to `NULL`.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.NumberSet.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.NumberSet.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.NumberSet.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.NumberSet.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.NumberSet.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.NumberSet.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.NumberSet.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.String","doc":"`:string` – `S`. Atoms (other than booleans/nil) are accepted on dump and become strings.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.String.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.String.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.String.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.String.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.String.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.String.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.String.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.StringSet","doc":"`:string_set` – `SS`. Empty sets dump to `NULL` (DynamoDB rejects empty sets).","ref":"Dynamo.Type.StringSet.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.StringSet.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.StringSet.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.StringSet.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.StringSet.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.StringSet.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.StringSet.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.Time","doc":"`:time` – `S` ISO 8601 time.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Time.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Time.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Time.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Time.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Time.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.Time.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.Time.html#load/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Dynamo.Type.UTCDateTime","doc":"`:utc_datetime` – `S` ISO 8601 with `Z`. Stored in UTC; sorts lexicographically.","ref":"Dynamo.Type.UTCDateTime.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.UTCDateTime.cast/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.UTCDateTime.html#cast/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.UTCDateTime.dump/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.UTCDateTime.html#dump/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Dynamo.Type.UTCDateTime.load/1","doc":"","ref":"Dynamo.Type.UTCDateTime.html#load/1"},{"type":"extras","title":"Dynamo","doc":"# Dynamo\n\n[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)\n\n> An Ecto-inspired Repo and schema DSL for Amazon DynamoDB.\n\nDynamo gives you typed schemas, composite key generation, a supervised `Repo`\nthat owns credentials and retries, pure request builders you can unit-test,\nand a single normalised `%Dynamo.Error{}` for every failure.\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.Order do\n  use Dynamo.Schema\n\n  item do\n    table \"app_data\"\n\n    field :user_id, :string, partition_key: true\n    field :placed_at, :utc_datetime, sort_key: true\n    field :order_id, :string, sort_key: true\n    field :total, :decimal\n    field :status, :string, default: \"pending\"\n    field :version, :integer, default: 0\n\n    global_secondary_index \"StatusIndex\", partition_key: :status, sort_key: :placed_at\n  end\nend\n\ndefmodule MyApp.Dynamo do\n  use Dynamo.Repo, otp_app: :my_app\nend\n\n{:ok, order} = MyApp.Dynamo.put(%MyApp.Order{user_id: \"u1\", placed_at: DateTime.utc_now(), order_id: \"o1\", total: Decimal.new(\"9.99\")})\n{:ok, page}  = MyApp.Dynamo.query(%MyApp.Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, sort_key: {:gte, \"2024-01-01\"}, limit: 20)\n{:ok, nil}   = MyApp.Dynamo.update(order, status: \"shipped\", version: {:increment, 1})\n```","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Installation - Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\ndef deps do\n  [\n    {:dynamo, github: \"bmalum/dynamo\"},\n    {:decimal, \"~> 2.0\"}   # optional, for the :decimal type\n  ]\nend\n```\n\nRequires Elixir 1.16+. `decimal` is optional: if you add it *after* `dynamo`\nwas first compiled, run `mix deps.compile dynamo --force` so the `:decimal`\ntype picks it up.\n\n> **Upgrading from 0.1?** The API changed completely. See [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md).","ref":"readme.html#installation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Setup - Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\n# lib/my_app/dynamo.ex\ndefmodule MyApp.Dynamo do\n  use Dynamo.Repo, otp_app: :my_app\nend\n\n# config/runtime.exs\nconfig :my_app, MyApp.Dynamo,\n  region: System.get_env(\"AWS_REGION\", \"eu-central-1\"),\n  endpoint: System.get_env(\"DYNAMO_ENDPOINT\")        # e.g. \"http://localhost:8000\" for DynamoDB Local\n\n# lib/my_app/application.ex\nchildren = [MyApp.Dynamo, ...]\n```\n\nCredentials resolve in the standard order: repo config → `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`/`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`\n→ ECS container credentials → EC2 instance metadata (IMDSv2). Metadata credentials\nare cached in a supervised process and refreshed before expiry.\n\nOther repo options: `:max_retries` (3), `:base_backoff_ms`, `:max_backoff_ms`,\n`:receive_timeout`, `:connect_timeout`, `:req_options`, `:telemetry_prefix`, `:batch_retries` (5).","ref":"readme.html#setup"},{"type":"extras","title":"Schemas - Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.User do\n  use Dynamo.Schema,\n    key_separator: \"#\",         # default\n    partition_key_name: \"pk\",   # default\n    sort_key_name: \"sk\"         # default\n\n  item do\n    table \"app_data\"\n    entity_name \"user\"          # default: underscored module basename; or a parent schema module\n\n    field :id, :string, partition_key: true\n    field :email, :string, sort_key: true\n    field :name, :string\n    field :age, :integer, default: 0\n    field :active, :boolean, default: true\n    field :created_at, :utc_datetime\n    field :balance, :decimal\n    field :tags, :string_set\n    field :profile, :map\n    field :avatar, :binary\n\n    global_secondary_index \"EmailIndex\", partition_key: :email, projection: :keys_only\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#schemas"},{"type":"extras","title":"Field types - Dynamo","doc":"| Type | Elixir | DynamoDB |\n|---|---|---|\n| `:string` (default) | `String.t()` | `S` |\n| `:integer`, `:float`, `:decimal` | `integer`, `float`, `Decimal.t()` | `N` |\n| `:boolean` | `boolean` | `BOOL` |\n| `:binary` | `binary` | `B` |\n| `:utc_datetime`, `:naive_datetime`, `:date`, `:time` | calendar structs (ISO 8601) | `S` |\n| `:map`, `:list` | string-keyed map, list | `M`, `L` |\n| `:string_set`, `:number_set`, `:binary_set` | `MapSet.t()` | `SS`, `NS`, `BS` |\n| `:any` | inferred | any |\n| `{:list, type}` | `[type]` | `L` |\n| `:vector`, `{:vector, n}` | `[float]` embedding | `L` of `N` |\n| a schema module | embedded struct (see below) | `M` |\n| a module | implements `Dynamo.Type` | your choice |\n\nField options: `default:`, `partition_key:`, `sort_key:`, `required:`.\n\nNil fields are **omitted** from written items (`omit_nil: true`, the default), so\n`put` never stores `NULL` attributes and `load` fills them from struct defaults.\nTo *remove* an attribute from an existing item use `update(item, field: :remove)`;\n`update(item, field: nil)` writes an explicit `NULL`.","ref":"readme.html#field-types"},{"type":"extras","title":"Embedded schemas - Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.Address do\n  use Dynamo.Schema, embedded: true      # no table, keys or indexes\n\n  item do\n    field :street, :string\n    field :city, :string\n    field :geo, {:list, :float}\n  end\nend\n\nfield :address, MyApp.Address\nfield :previous_addresses, {:list, MyApp.Address}\n```\n\nEmbedded values keep their types on the way back (dates stay dates, decimals\nstay decimals). Any table schema can be embedded too; its key attributes are\nleft out when nested.","ref":"readme.html#embedded-schemas"},{"type":"extras","title":"Keys - Dynamo","doc":"Key fields are combined in declaration order with `key_separator`:\n\n```\npk = \" # \"      e.g. \"user#u1\"\nsk = \" \"                    e.g. \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z#o1\"\n```\n\nUse `partition_key [:a, :b]` / `sort_key [:c, :d]` inside `item` instead of\nper-field flags if you prefer. Rules that keep keys round-trippable:\n\n- Every partition key field must be non-nil → otherwise `{:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :validation_error}}`.\n- Sort key fields may be *partially* populated: generation stops at the first\n  `nil`, producing a prefix for `begins_with` queries.\n- A key value containing the separator is rejected (this is why the default is\n  `\"#\"`, not `\"-\"` – ISO dates contain dashes).\n\n**Existing tables that don't follow this layout:** `use Dynamo.Schema, raw_keys: true`\nuses the partition/sort key fields as-is (native types, no entity prefix).","ref":"readme.html#keys"},{"type":"extras","title":"Working with schemas directly - Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\n{:ok, %Dynamo.Key{pk: %{\"S\" => \"user#u1\"}, sk: %{\"S\" => \"a@b.c\"}}} = Dynamo.Schema.primary_key(user)\n{:ok, item}   = Dynamo.Schema.dump(user)          # DynamoDB item map incl. pk/sk\n{:ok, user}   = Dynamo.Schema.load(MyApp.User, item)\n```","ref":"readme.html#working-with-schemas-directly"},{"type":"extras","title":"Operations - Dynamo","doc":"All return `{:ok, result} | {:error, %Dynamo.Error{}}`; every function has a\n`!` variant that raises.\n\n```elixir\nalias MyApp.{Dynamo, User}\n\n# write\n{:ok, user} = Dynamo.put(user)\n{:ok, user} = Dynamo.put(user, condition: \"attribute_not_exists(pk)\")\n{:ok, old}  = Dynamo.put(user, return_values: :all_old)\n\n# read\n{:ok, %User{} | nil} = Dynamo.get(%User{id: \"u1\", email: \"a@b.c\"}, consistent: true)\n\n# update – SET / REMOVE / ADD / DELETE built for you\n{:ok, nil} = Dynamo.update(%User{id: \"u1\", email: \"a@b.c\"},\n  name: \"Jane\",\n  age: {:increment, 1},\n  tags: {:add, MapSet.new([\"vip\"])},\n  legacy_field: :remove,\n  login_count: {:if_not_exists, 0}\n)\n{:ok, %User{}} = Dynamo.update(key, [age: {:add, 1}], return_values: :all_new)\n\n# delete\n{:ok, nil}     = Dynamo.delete(%User{id: \"u1\", email: \"a@b.c\"})\n{:ok, %User{}} = Dynamo.delete(key, return_values: :all_old)\n```\n\nExpression options (`condition:`, `filter:`, `projection:`, `names:`, `values:`)\nare the same everywhere. `condition:` and `filter:` take either a raw string\n(with your own `names:`/`values:`, which are plain Elixir values encoded for you)\nor a keyword DSL that generates the placeholders:\n\n```elixir\nDynamo.put(user, condition: \"#v = :v\", names: %{\"#v\" => \"version\"}, values: %{v: 3})\nDynamo.put(user, condition: [version: 3])                                     # same thing\nDynamo.put(user, condition: [pk: :not_exists])\nDynamo.update(key, [age: {:increment, 1}], condition: [age: {:lt, 120}, active: true])\nDynamo.query(order, filter: {:or, [status: \"open\"], [total: {:gte, 100}]})\nDynamo.scan(User, filter: [tags: {:contains, \"vip\"}, {[:address, :city], \"Berlin\"}])   # nested path\n```\n\nOperators: value (`=`), `{:eq | :ne | :lt | :lte | :gt | :gte, v}`, `{:between, lo, hi}`,\n`{:in, [..]}`, `{:begins_with, s}`, `{:contains, v}`, `:exists`, `:not_exists`,\n`{:attribute_type, \"S\"}`, `{:size, {:gt, n}}`; combinators `{:and, a, b}`, `{:or, a, b}`, `{:not, a}`.\nValues are dumped with the field's schema type.","ref":"readme.html#operations"},{"type":"extras","title":"Querying - Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\n# all items in the partition\n{:ok, %Dynamo.Page{items: items, last_evaluated_key: key}} = Dynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"})\n\n# sort key conditions\nDynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, sort_key: {:begins_with, \"2024-01\"})\nDynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, sort_key: {:between, \"2024-01-01\", \"2024-02-01\"})\nDynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, sort_key: {:gte, \"2024-06\"}, descending: true, limit: 10)\n\n# populated sort-key fields on the struct imply begins_with on the partial key\nDynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\", placed_at: ~U[2024-01-15 00:00:00Z]})\n\n# pagination\n{:ok, page1} = Dynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, limit: 50)\n{:ok, page2} = Dynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, limit: 50, start_key: page1.last_evaluated_key)\n\n# global secondary index (keys use the field's own type)\nDynamo.query(%Order{status: \"shipped\"}, index: \"StatusIndex\", sort_key: {:gt, ~U[2024-01-01 00:00:00Z]})\n\n# filter / projection / count\nDynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, filter: \"#t > :min\", names: %{\"#t\" => \"total\"}, values: %{min: 100})\nDynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, projection: [:order_id, :total])\nDynamo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, select: :count)\n\n# everything, paginating for you (bounded by :limit)\n{:ok, orders} = Dynamo.query_all(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, limit: 1_000)\n```\n\n`%Dynamo.Page{}` is enumerable: `Enum.map(page, & &1.total)`.","ref":"readme.html#querying"},{"type":"extras","title":"Streaming and scans - Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\n# lazy query\nDynamo.stream(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, page_size: 100)\n|> Stream.filter(&(&1.status == \"open\"))\n|> Enum.take(10)\n\n# lazy scan\nDynamo.stream(User) |> Enum.each(&migrate/1)\n\n# truly parallel scan: segments fetched concurrently under the repo's Task.Supervisor\nDynamo.stream(User, segments: 8, max_concurrency: 4) |> Enum.count()\n\n# one page\n{:ok, %Dynamo.Page{}} = Dynamo.scan(User, limit: 100, filter: \"attribute_exists(email)\")\n```\n\nStreams raise `%Dynamo.Error{}` on failure (there is no other way to signal\nfrom inside a stream). Scans read every item – stream lazily, but don't scan casually.","ref":"readme.html#streaming-and-scans"},{"type":"extras","title":"Batches - Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\n# any number of items, chunked into 25, unprocessed items retried with backoff\n{:ok, %{unprocessed: []}} = Dynamo.batch_write(users ++ [{:delete, old_user}])\n\n# any number of keys (one schema), chunked into 100\n{:ok, %{items: users, unprocessed_keys: []}} = Dynamo.batch_get([%User{id: \"u1\", email: \"a\"}, %User{id: \"u2\", email: \"b\"}])\n```","ref":"readme.html#batches"},{"type":"extras","title":"Vector search - Dynamo","doc":"DynamoDB has native vector indexes (August 2026). Declare one on a `{:vector, n}`\nfield and search it with an embedding:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.Doc do\n  use Dynamo.Schema\n\n  item do\n    table \"docs\"\n    field :id, :string, partition_key: true\n    field :tenant, :string\n    field :lang, :string\n    field :title, :string\n    field :embedding, {:vector, 1024}\n\n    vector_index \"Semantic\",\n      field: :embedding,\n      distance: :cosine,                          # :cosine | :dot_product | :euclidean\n      projection: :include, projected_attributes: [:title, :lang],\n      partition_key: :tenant,                     # optional: scopes and scales searches\n      filters: [:lang]                            # optional inline filter attributes\n  end\nend\n\n{:ok, %{results: results}} =\n  Dynamo.search_vectors(MyApp.Doc, \"Semantic\", query_embedding,\n    top_k: 5,\n    filter: [tenant: \"acme\", lang: \"en\"]          # partition key is required when declared\n  )\n\nfor {%MyApp.Doc{title: t}, score} <- results, do: IO.puts(\"#{score}  #{t}\")\n```\n\n`mix dynamo.create_table --schema MyApp.Doc` creates the index (on-demand billing\nis required). Results are `{struct, score}` pairs, most similar first; lower is\ncloser for `:cosine`/`:euclidean`, higher for `:dot_product`. Only projected\nattributes are returned; key fields are recovered from the item key. Writes to the\nindex are eventually consistent. `SearchVectors` is served from a separate AWS\nendpoint, which the client routes automatically (`:search_endpoint` to override).","ref":"readme.html#vector-search"},{"type":"extras","title":"Transactions - Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\n{:ok, _} =\n  Dynamo.transaction(\n    [\n      {:update, %Account{id: \"src\"}, [balance: {:decrement, 100}], condition: \"#b >= :amt\", names: %{\"#b\" => \"balance\"}, values: %{amt: 100}},\n      {:update, %Account{id: \"dst\"}, [balance: {:increment, 100}]},\n      {:put, %Transfer{id: \"t1\", amount: 100}, condition: \"attribute_not_exists(pk)\"},\n      {:check, %Account{id: \"audit\"}, \"attribute_exists(pk)\"},\n      {:delete, %Hold{id: \"h1\"}}\n    ],\n    client_request_token: \"transfer-t1\"   # idempotency (10 min window)\n  )\n```\n\nOn cancellation the error carries per-item reasons:\n\n```elixir\n{:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :transaction_canceled, cancellation_reasons: [%{code: \"ConditionalCheckFailed\"}, %{code: \"None\"}, ...]}}\n```","ref":"readme.html#transactions"},{"type":"extras","title":"Errors - Dynamo","doc":"Every failure is a `%Dynamo.Error{}`:\n\n```elixir\ncase Dynamo.put(user, condition: \"attribute_not_exists(pk)\") do\n  {:ok, user} -> ...\n  {:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :conditional_check_failed}} -> {:error, :already_exists}\n  {:error, %Dynamo.Error{retryable?: true}} -> retry_later()\n  {:error, %Dynamo.Error{} = e} -> Logger.error(Exception.message(e))\nend\n```\n\nFields: `type`, `message`, `aws_type` (e.g. `\"ResourceNotFoundException\"`), `status`,\n`retryable?`, `cancellation_reasons`, `details`.\n\nCommon types: `:validation_error` (local or AWS), `:resource_not_found`,\n`:conditional_check_failed`, `:provisioned_throughput_exceeded`, `:throttled`,\n`:access_denied`, `:authentication_error`, `:transaction_canceled`,\n`:transaction_conflict`, `:item_collection_size_exceeded`, `:internal_server_error`,\n`:transport_error`, `:decode_error`. Retryable errors are retried by the client\nautomatically (`:max_retries`, jittered exponential backoff).\n\n**Retries and idempotency.** Throttling and 5xx responses are safe to retry –\nDynamoDB did not apply the write. A *transport* timeout is different: the\nrequest may or may not have been applied, and the client retries it anyway\n(as the AWS SDKs do). Plain `put`/`delete` are idempotent so this is harmless;\n`update` with `{:increment, n}`/`{:add, n}` is not. For counters that must be\nexact, guard the update with a version condition\n(`update(item, [count: {:increment, 1}, version: {:increment, 1}], condition: [version: item.version])`)\nor use `transaction/2` with `client_request_token:`, which DynamoDB de-duplicates\nfor 10 minutes. Set `max_retries: 0` on the repo to opt out of retries entirely.","ref":"readme.html#errors"},{"type":"extras","title":"Telemetry - Dynamo","doc":"The client emits `[:dynamo, :request, :start | :stop | :exception]` (prefix\nconfigurable) with metadata `action`, `table`, `attempt`, `result`, `status`,\n`error`, `consumed_capacity` and `duration` on stop:\n\n```elixir\n:telemetry.attach(\"dynamo-log\", [:dynamo, :request, :stop], fn _, %{duration: d}, meta, _ ->\n  Logger.debug(\"dynamo #{meta.action} #{meta.table} #{System.convert_time_unit(d, :native, :millisecond)}ms #{meta.result}\")\nend, nil)\n```\n\nAdd `return_consumed_capacity: :total` to any call to get capacity in the metadata.","ref":"readme.html#telemetry"},{"type":"extras","title":"Mix tasks - Dynamo","doc":"```bash\nmix dynamo.create_table --schema MyApp.User --endpoint http://localhost:8000   # table + GSIs + vector indexes from the schema\nmix dynamo.create_table my_table --partition-key id --no-sort-key --region eu-west-1\nmix dynamo.list_tables --name-contains user\nmix dynamo.delete_table my_table --force\nmix dynamo.generate_schema legacy_table --module MyApp.Legacy                   # round-trip safe: detects key layout\n```\n\nAll tasks load your application config, accept `--repo MyApp.Dynamo` to reuse a\nstarted repo's client, and exit non-zero on failure.","ref":"readme.html#mix-tasks"},{"type":"extras","title":"Testing your application - Dynamo","doc":"Point the repo at a fake via `Req`'s plug option – no network, no mocks of library modules:\n\n```elixir\nconfig :my_app, MyApp.Dynamo,\n  region: \"us-east-1\", access_key_id: \"test\", secret_access_key: \"test\",\n  req_options: [plug: {Req.Test, MyApp.Dynamo}]\n```\n\nOr run [DynamoDB Local](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/DynamoDBLocal.html)\nand set `endpoint: \"http://localhost:8000\"`. The library's own test suite uses an\nin-memory fake (`test/support/fake_dynamo.ex`) you can borrow.","ref":"readme.html#testing-your-application"},{"type":"extras","title":"Design - Dynamo","doc":"- **Schema** – typed fields, one `Dynamo.Schema.primary_key/1` used by every operation.\n- **Request** – pure builders (`Dynamo.Request`, `Dynamo.Update`) that return `{action, payload}`; fully unit-tested against golden JSON.\n- **Client** – SigV4, retries, telemetry, error normalisation. Nothing above it sees a raw AWS error.\n- **Repo** – supervised owner of client + credentials; the only stateful piece.\n- **Fail loud** – nil keys, separator collisions, unknown options and wrong types are errors, never sentinels.\n\nSee [Agents.md](Agents.md) for data-modelling guidance and the `guides/` folder for worked examples.","ref":"readme.html#design"},{"type":"extras","title":"Contributing - Dynamo","doc":"See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Security issues: [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).","ref":"readme.html#contributing"},{"type":"extras","title":"License - Dynamo","doc":"MIT – see [LICENSE](LICENSE).","ref":"readme.html#license"},{"type":"extras","title":"Changelog","doc":"# Changelog","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"0.2.0 – unreleased - Changelog","doc":"Complete rewrite. **Every public API changed.** The 0.1 line was a beta whose\ndocumented API did not match its implementation; 0.2 is what the docs promised.","ref":"changelog.html#0-2-0-unreleased"},{"type":"extras","title":"Architecture - Changelog","doc":"- **`Dynamo.Repo`** – `use Dynamo.Repo, otp_app: :my_app` defines a supervised\n  repository that owns region, endpoint, credentials, retry policy and a\n  `Task.Supervisor`. All operations are called on the repo. `Dynamo.Table`,\n  `Dynamo.AWS`, `Dynamo.DynamoDB`, `Dynamo.Config`, `Dynamo.Logger`,\n  `Dynamo.Helper`, `Dynamo.ErrorHandler`, `Dynamo.Transaction`,\n  `Dynamo.Table.Stream(.Producer)` and `Dynamo.Encoder/Decoder` are removed.\n- **Typed fields** – `field :name, :type, opts`. 16 built-in types incl.\n  `:utc_datetime`, `:decimal`, `:binary`, sets; `Dynamo.Type` behaviour for\n  custom types. Encoding/decoding is schema-driven and round-trips.\n- **`Dynamo.Request`** – pure request builders returning `{action, payload}`,\n  unit-tested against the DynamoDB JSON shapes.\n- **`Dynamo.Client`** – SigV4 (correct `Host` with port), jittered exponential\n  retry for retryable errors, `:telemetry` events, error normalisation.\n- **`Dynamo.Credentials`** – static → env → ECS → IMDSv2 chain with a supervised,\n  single-flight refreshing cache.\n- **`Dynamo.Error`** – the only error type. AWS `__type`s are un-namespaced and\n  both `message`/`Message` are read, so `:resource_not_found`,\n  `:conditional_check_failed`, `:provisioned_throughput_exceeded`,\n  `:transaction_canceled` (with `cancellation_reasons`) etc. actually match.\n- **`Dynamo.Page`** – uniform result for `query`/`scan` with `last_evaluated_key`;\n  `Enumerable`.\n- **`Dynamo.Stream`** – lazy query/scan; `segments:` runs a genuinely parallel\n  scan with bounded concurrency and backpressure.\n- **`Dynamo.Update`** – SET/REMOVE/ADD/DELETE with `{:increment, n}`,\n  `{:decrement, n}`, `{:add, _}`, `{:delete, set}`, `{:append, l}`,\n  `{:prepend, l}`, `{:if_not_exists, v}`, `:remove`.\n- **`Dynamo.Condition`** – keyword/combinator DSL accepted by every\n  `condition:`/`filter:` option; generates names/values with the field's type.\n- **Embedded schemas** – `use Dynamo.Schema, embedded: true`; every schema is a\n  `Dynamo.Type`, so `field :address, MyApp.Address` and\n  `field :items, {:list, MyApp.Item}` round-trip with full typing.\n- **`{:list, type}`** parameterised lists.\n- **Vector search** – `{:vector, n}` field type, `vector_index` in the schema\n  DSL (distance, projection, partition key, inline filters),\n  `Repo.search_vectors/4`, `create_table --schema` emits `VectorIndexes`, and\n  the client routes `SearchVectors` to AWS's separate search endpoint.\n- `load/2` recovers key fields from `pk`/`sk` when a projection omitted them\n  (keys-only GSIs, vector indexes).\n- `entity_name ParentModule` – compile-time link for parent/child items.\n- `table/1` accepts compile-time expressions.\n- `mix dynamo.create_table --schema A --schema B` merges GSIs of a single-table design.\n- Credentials cache read path is lock-free (`:persistent_term`); only refreshes\n  go through the GenServer.\n- CI workflow (unit matrix + live suite against DynamoDB Local).","ref":"changelog.html#architecture"},{"type":"extras","title":"Bugs fixed (from the 0.1 review) - Changelog","doc":"- Composite sort keys were corrupted when a value contained the separator\n  (`2024-01-15` with `-` became `2024-15`). Keys are now built from values\n  directly; separator collisions are rejected.\n- Composite partition key fields declared with `field ..., partition_key: true`\n  were emitted in reverse order.\n- Nil partition-key fields silently became the string `\"empty\"`; now a\n  `:validation_error`.\n- AWS errors were never categorised (namespaced `__type`, lowercase `message`).\n- Transaction update operators produced invalid expressions (`SET a + :v`) and\n  expression attributes passed as documented were dropped.\n- `belongs_to` keys were applied in get/query but not delete/update/batch\n  get/transactions. `belongs_to` is removed; use `entity_name ParentModule`\n  (resolved at compile time) plus a typed sort key with a default prefix\n  (see guides/DATA_MODELLING.md).\n- Encoder/decoder treated any map with a key like `\"S\"`/`\"N\"`/`\"M\"` as an\n  already-encoded value, corrupting user data both ways. Pre-encoded values must\n  now be wrapped in `Dynamo.Raw`.\n- Binaries were typed `S` or `B` depending on UTF-8 validity; `:binary` is now\n  explicit and stable.\n- `:client` was ignored by query/batch write/parallel scan/streams; the repo owns\n  the client so every call uses the same configuration.\n- ETS credential cache was created lazily by arbitrary processes (race,\n  destroyed on owner exit); replaced by a supervised GenServer.\n- Batch writes reported total failure as `{:ok, processed_items: 0}`; hard\n  errors are now returned, `UnprocessedItems` retried with backoff.\n- `list_items` could not paginate; `query/2` returns `%Dynamo.Page{}`.\n- Query accumulation was O(n²) and unbounded; streams are lazy.\n- \"Parallel\" streaming was sequential `Stream.concat`; `scan_to_process` used an\n  un-awaited linked `Task.async` and mis-wrapped batch messages;\n  `producer_spec/2` called a non-existent function. All replaced by\n  `Dynamo.Stream`.\n- `Dynamo.Logger` wrote full item payloads to stdout on success only; replaced\n  by telemetry.\n- Mix tasks did not load the host app config, exited 0 on failure, and\n  `generate_schema` produced schemas that could not read the source table.\n  Fixed; `create_table --schema` derives keys and GSIs from a schema.\n- `lib/examples.ex` shipped example schemas in the library namespace; removed.\n- Tests: `table_stream_test.exs` did not compile; `mock`/meck removed in favour\n  of `Req.Test` plugs and an in-memory fake; property-based round-trip tests for\n  all types; golden tests for every request builder.","ref":"changelog.html#bugs-fixed-from-the-0-1-review"},{"type":"extras","title":"Migration - Changelog","doc":"| 0.1 | 0.2 |\n|---|---|\n| `Dynamo.Table.put_item(s)` | `MyRepo.put(s)` |\n| `Dynamo.Table.get_item(s)` | `MyRepo.get(s)` (full key required) |\n| `Dynamo.Table.list_items(s, sk_operator: :begins_with, sort_key: v)` | `MyRepo.query(s, sort_key: {:begins_with, v})` → `%Dynamo.Page{}` |\n| `Dynamo.Table.list_items(s, index_name: \"X\")` | `MyRepo.query(s, index: \"X\")` |\n| `Dynamo.Table.update_item(s, %{a: 1})` | `MyRepo.update(s, a: 1)` |\n| `Dynamo.Table.batch_write_item(list)` | `MyRepo.batch_write(list)` |\n| `Dynamo.Table.parallel_scan(M, segments: 4)` | `MyRepo.stream(M, segments: 4)` |\n| `Dynamo.Table.Stream.scan(M)` | `MyRepo.stream(M)` |\n| `Dynamo.Transaction.transact([...])` | `MyRepo.transaction([...])` (ops now `{:put, s, opts}` etc.) |\n| `table_name \"t\"` | `table \"t\"` |\n| `field :x` (untyped) | `field :x, :string` (or the real type) |\n| `belongs_to :parent, P, sk_strategy: :prefix` | `entity_name P` + `field :kind, :string, sort_key: true, default: \"child\"` |\n| `Dynamo.Config.put_process_config/1` | repo config / `use Dynamo.Schema, opts` |\n| `Dynamo.Logger.enable/0` | attach to `[:dynamo, :request, :stop]` |\n\nStored keys are compatible for schemas that used the default `#` separator,\nsingle-field keys, default `pk`/`sk` names **and single-word module names**.\nThe default entity name is now `Macro.underscore/1` of the module basename\n(`UserProfile` → `\"user_profile\"`); 0.1 lower-cased it (`\"userprofile\"`).\nSet `entity_name \"userprofile\"` explicitly on such schemas to keep reading\nexisting data. Composite sort keys written by 0.1 with values containing the\nseparator are corrupted and must be re-written.","ref":"changelog.html#migration"},{"type":"extras","title":"0.1.x - Changelog","doc":"Initial beta.","ref":"changelog.html#0-1-x"},{"type":"extras","title":"Contributing","doc":"# Contributing\n\nThanks for looking at Dynamo. Bug reports, questions and pull requests are welcome.","ref":"contributing.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Before you open a pull request - Contributing","doc":"- Open an issue first for anything that changes the public API or adds a\n  DynamoDB feature, so the shape can be agreed before code is written.\n- Read `Agents.md` for the mental model and `skills/dynamo-maintainer/SKILL.md`\n  for the invariants, the test tiers and the step-by-step procedure for adding\n  a feature. The maintainer skill is written for AI agents and applies to\n  humans just the same.","ref":"contributing.html#before-you-open-a-pull-request"},{"type":"extras","title":"Running the checks - Contributing","doc":"```bash\nmix deps.get\nmix format --check-formatted\nMIX_ENV=test mix compile --force --warnings-as-errors\nmix test\nmix docs\n```\n\nAll four must be clean. The unit suite runs against an in-memory fake\n(`test/support/fake_dynamo.ex`) and takes about a second.\n\nChanges that touch the wire (new request, new attribute type, endpoint routing)\nalso need a scenario in `test/integration/live_test.exs`. It runs against\nDynamoDB Local or a real AWS account and cleans up its own tables:\n\n```bash\nDYNAMO_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8000 AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=local AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=local \\\n  mix test --include integration test/integration/live_test.exs\n```","ref":"contributing.html#running-the-checks"},{"type":"extras","title":"What a good pull request looks like - Contributing","doc":"- One change per PR, with a test that fails without it.\n- Request builders get a golden-payload test; schema DSL changes get a\n  compile-error test for the failure case.\n- Documentation updated in the same PR: README section, `Agents.md` cheat\n  sheet, the relevant guide, and a `CHANGELOG.md` line under \"unreleased\".\n  Every snippet in the docs must run.\n- No new dependencies without discussion. Runtime deps are `req` and `jason`;\n  `decimal` is optional and must stay optional.","ref":"contributing.html#what-a-good-pull-request-looks-like"},{"type":"extras","title":"Style - Contributing","doc":"`mix format` decides. Beyond that: public functions return\n`{:ok, value} | {:error, %Dynamo.Error{}}`, options are validated with\n`Keyword.validate/2`, invalid input is an error and never a sentinel value.","ref":"contributing.html#style"},{"type":"extras","title":"Reporting a security issue - Contributing","doc":"See [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md). Please don't open a public issue for it.","ref":"contributing.html#reporting-a-security-issue"},{"type":"extras","title":"Security","doc":"# Security","ref":"security.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Supported versions - Security","doc":"Only the latest 0.x release receives fixes. 0.1.x is unsupported.","ref":"security.html#supported-versions"},{"type":"extras","title":"Reporting a vulnerability - Security","doc":"Please report security issues privately through\n[GitHub's private vulnerability reporting](https://github.com/bmalum/dynamo/security/advisories/new).\nDo not open a public issue.\n\nInclude the library version, a description of the issue and, if possible, a\nminimal reproduction. You will get an acknowledgement within a few days and a\nfix or a written assessment as soon as one exists. Credit is given in the\nadvisory and the changelog unless you prefer otherwise.","ref":"security.html#reporting-a-vulnerability"},{"type":"extras","title":"Scope - Security","doc":"Dynamo signs requests with your AWS credentials and sends them to DynamoDB.\nThings that are in scope:\n\n- credential handling (`Dynamo.Credentials`, the cache, IMDS/ECS lookups)\n- request signing and endpoint selection\n- anything that could make the library send data somewhere other than the\n  configured endpoint, or log or expose credentials\n\nOut of scope: vulnerabilities in DynamoDB itself, in `req`/`finch`/`jason`\n(report upstream), and misconfiguration of IAM policies in your account.","ref":"security.html#scope"},{"type":"extras","title":"LICENSE","doc":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2024-2026 Martin Karrer\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.","ref":"license.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"# Dynamo Agent Guide\n\nA concise reference for AI agents and developers using the Dynamo library. Every\nsnippet here compiles against the current API; if something in this file\ndisagrees with the code, the code is right and this file has a bug.","ref":"agents.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Mental model - Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"```\nSchema  – typed fields + key layout. Pure. `Dynamo.Schema.primary_key/1`, `dump/1`, `load/2`.\nRequest – pure builders: struct + opts -> {action, payload}. `Dynamo.Request`, `Dynamo.Update`.\nClient  – SigV4, retries, telemetry, error normalisation. `Dynamo.Client`.\nRepo    – supervised owner of client + credentials. The thing you call. `use Dynamo.Repo`.\n```\n\nAll operations return `{:ok, value} | {:error, %Dynamo.Error{}}`. Nothing above\nthe client ever sees a raw AWS error map.","ref":"agents.html#mental-model"},{"type":"extras","title":"Defining a schema - Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.Order do\n  use Dynamo.Schema                       # opts: key_separator, partition_key_name, sort_key_name,\n                                          #       prefix_sort_key, raw_keys, omit_nil\n  item do\n    table \"app\"\n    entity_name \"order\"                   # default: underscored module basename\n\n    field :user_id, :string, partition_key: true\n    field :placed_at, :utc_datetime, sort_key: true\n    field :order_id, :string, sort_key: true\n    field :total, :decimal\n    field :status, :string, default: \"pending\"\n    field :version, :integer, default: 0\n\n    global_secondary_index \"StatusIndex\", partition_key: :status, sort_key: :placed_at\n  end\nend\n```\n\nTypes: `:string :integer :float :decimal :boolean :binary :utc_datetime\n:naive_datetime :date :time :map :list :string_set :number_set :binary_set :any`,\n`{:list, type}`, `{:vector, n}` (embedding), an embedded schema module\n(`use Dynamo.Schema, embedded: true`), or a module implementing `Dynamo.Type`.\n\nNil fields are omitted on write (`omit_nil: true`); `update(item, f: :remove)`\ndeletes an attribute, `update(item, f: nil)` writes `NULL`.\n\nGenerated keys: `pk = \"order# \"`, `sk = \" # \"`.\nAlternative: `partition_key [:a, :b]` / `sort_key [:c, :d]` instead of per-field flags.\n\nCompile-time errors for: missing `table`, no partition key, unknown option,\nunknown type, undefined field in a key/index, duplicate field/index.","ref":"agents.html#defining-a-schema"},{"type":"extras","title":"Defining a repo - Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.Dynamo do\n  use Dynamo.Repo, otp_app: :my_app\nend\n\nconfig :my_app, MyApp.Dynamo, region: \"eu-central-1\", endpoint: System.get_env(\"DYNAMO_ENDPOINT\")\nchildren = [MyApp.Dynamo]\n```","ref":"agents.html#defining-a-repo"},{"type":"extras","title":"Operations cheat sheet - Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"```elixir\nalias MyApp.Dynamo, as: Repo\n\nRepo.put(struct, condition: \"attribute_not_exists(pk)\")           # {:ok, struct}\nRepo.put(struct, condition: [pk: :not_exists, status: {:in, [\"a\", \"b\"]}])   # DSL → same expression\nRepo.put(struct, return_values: :all_old)                          # {:ok, old | nil}\nRepo.get(%Order{user_id: \"u\", placed_at: dt, order_id: \"o\"})       # {:ok, struct | nil}; full key required\nRepo.get(key, consistent: true, projection: [:total])\nRepo.delete(key)                                                   # {:ok, nil}\nRepo.delete(key, return_values: :all_old)                          # {:ok, old | nil}\nRepo.update(key, status: \"paid\", version: {:increment, 1})         # {:ok, nil}\nRepo.update(key, [tags: {:add, MapSet.new([\"x\"])}, tmp: :remove], return_values: :all_new)\n\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\"})                                   # {:ok, %Dynamo.Page{}}\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\"}, sort_key: {:begins_with, \"2024-06\"})\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\"}, sort_key: {:between, \"2024-01-01\", \"2024-12-31~\"}, descending: true, limit: 50)\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\", placed_at: dt})                    # struct sk fields => begins_with on partial sk\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\", placed_at: dt}, sort_key: :none)   # ignore struct sk fields\nRepo.query(%Order{status: \"paid\"}, index: \"StatusIndex\", sort_key: {:gt, ~U[2024-01-01 00:00:00Z]})\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\"}, filter: \"#t > :m\", names: %{\"#t\" => \"total\"}, values: %{m: 100})\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\"}, filter: [total: {:gt, 100}])                # same, via Dynamo.Condition\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\"}, filter: {:or, [status: \"open\"], [total: {:gte, 100}]})\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\"}, limit: 50, start_key: page.last_evaluated_key)\nRepo.query_all(%Order{user_id: \"u\"}, limit: 1_000)                 # {:ok, [struct]}\n\nRepo.scan(Order, limit: 100)                                       # {:ok, %Dynamo.Page{}}\nRepo.stream(%Order{user_id: \"u\"}, page_size: 100)                  # lazy Stream (raises Dynamo.Error on failure)\nRepo.stream(Order, segments: 8, max_concurrency: 4)                # parallel scan\n\nRepo.batch_write(structs ++ [{:delete, s}])                        # {:ok, %{unprocessed: []}}\nRepo.batch_get([key1, key2])                                       # {:ok, %{items: [...], unprocessed_keys: []}}\n\nRepo.transaction([\n  {:update, %Acct{id: \"a\"}, [balance: {:decrement, 5}], condition: \"#b >= :v\", names: %{\"#b\" => \"balance\"}, values: %{v: 5}},\n  {:update, %Acct{id: \"b\"}, [balance: {:increment, 5}]},\n  {:put, %Ledger{id: \"l1\"}, condition: \"attribute_not_exists(pk)\"},\n  {:check, %Acct{id: \"c\"}, \"attribute_exists(pk)\"},\n  {:delete, %Hold{id: \"h\"}}\n], client_request_token: \"idem-1\")\n\n# vector search (schema declares `vector_index \"Semantic\", field: :embedding, partition_key: :tenant, filters: [:lang]`)\nRepo.search_vectors(Doc, \"Semantic\", embedding, top_k: 5, filter: [tenant: \"t\", lang: \"en\"])\n#=> {:ok, %{results: [{%Doc{}, score}, ...], consumed_capacity: ...}}\n\nRepo.request(\"DescribeTable\", %{\"TableName\" => \"app\"})              # raw escape hatch\n```\n\nUpdate operators: plain value, `{:increment, n}`, `{:decrement, n}`, `{:add, n | set}`,\n`{:delete, set}`, `{:append, list}`, `{:prepend, list}`, `{:if_not_exists, v}`, `:remove`.\nKey fields cannot be updated (error) – delete and re-put.\n\nExpression options everywhere: `condition:`/`filter:` (raw string, or a\n`Dynamo.Condition` DSL: keyword list = AND of `field: value | {op, v} | :exists | ...`,\n`{:and | :or, a, b}`, `{:not, a}`, nested path as list), `projection:` (string or\nfield list), `names:` (`%{\"#n\" => \"attr\"}`), `values:` (`%{v: elixir_value}`,\nencoded for you). `return_values: :none | :all_old | :all_new | :updated_old | :updated_new`.\n\nRetries: throttling/5xx are retried with backoff. Transport timeouts are retried\ntoo, so `{:increment, n}` updates can double-apply after a timeout – guard with a\nversion `condition:` or use `transaction/2` + `client_request_token:`.","ref":"agents.html#operations-cheat-sheet"},{"type":"extras","title":"Errors - Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"```elixir\n%Dynamo.Error{type: atom, message: String.t, aws_type: \"ConditionalCheckFailedException\" | nil,\n              status: 400 | nil, retryable?: boolean, cancellation_reasons: [...] | nil, details: term}\n```\n\nCommon `type`s: `:validation_error :resource_not_found :conditional_check_failed\n:provisioned_throughput_exceeded :throttled :access_denied :authentication_error\n:transaction_canceled :transaction_conflict :internal_server_error :transport_error\n:decode_error :no_credentials`. Retryable ones are retried by the client (3× default).\n\nLocal validation failures (nil partition key, separator in a key value, unknown\noption, wrong type, updating a key field, >25 batch items, duplicate items in a\ntransaction) return `{:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :validation_error}}` *before*\nany request is sent.","ref":"agents.html#errors"},{"type":"extras","title":"Modelling rules of thumb - Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"1. **List access patterns first.** Every query needs a partition key; design keys from queries, not from entities.\n2. **High-cardinality partition keys.** Never a date or status alone. Combine (`partition_key [:tenant, :customer_id]`) or shard.\n3. **Sort keys drive ranges.** Put the dimension you range over first (ISO 8601 datetimes sort correctly). Prefix with a type string for single-partition adjacency lists.\n4. **GSIs for the second and third pattern.** Keys keep their field type (numbers stay `N`). Use `:keys_only`/`:include` to cut cost. No consistent reads on GSIs.\n5. **Single table:** several schemas share `table \"app\"`; `entity_name` disambiguates the `pk`. Child items in the parent's partition: `entity_name ParentModule` (compile-time link) + `field :kind, :string, sort_key: true, default: \"child\"`.\n6. **Items < 400 KB.** Store blobs in S3, keep the reference.\n7. **Unbounded lists don't belong in one item.** One item per element with a composite sort key.\n8. **Scans are for migrations.** They read every item; `stream/2` bounds memory, not cost.\n9. **Idempotency:** `client_request_token:` on transactions; `condition: \"attribute_not_exists(pk)\"` on creates.\n10. **Vectors:** `{:vector, n}` field + `vector_index`; `:cosine` for unnormalised embeddings, `:dot_product` for unit vectors. Add `partition_key:` to scope searches to a tenant (required in the filter). On-demand billing only; searches are eventually consistent.\n11. **Fail loud:** the library never writes `\"empty\"` or silently drops data. If you get a `:validation_error`, fix the data or the schema.","ref":"agents.html#modelling-rules-of-thumb"},{"type":"extras","title":"Testing - Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"- Request building is pure: assert on `Dynamo.Request.*` output directly.\n- Stub HTTP with `req_options: [plug: {Req.Test, MyRepo}]` in the repo config, or\n  copy `test/support/fake_dynamo.ex` (in-memory DynamoDB) from this repo.\n- Set `consolidate_protocols: Mix.env() != :test` in `mix.exs` if schemas are defined in tests.","ref":"agents.html#testing"},{"type":"extras","title":"Mix tasks - Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"```\nmix dynamo.create_table --schema MyApp.Order [--repo MyApp.Dynamo | --endpoint URL --region R]\nmix dynamo.create_table NAME --partition-key id --no-sort-key\nmix dynamo.list_tables [--name-contains x]\nmix dynamo.delete_table NAME [--force]\nmix dynamo.generate_schema NAME [--module M] [--output path] [--overwrite]\n```\n\nAll exit non-zero on failure and honour the application's config.","ref":"agents.html#mix-tasks"},{"type":"extras","title":"Maintaining the library itself - Dynamo Agent Guide","doc":"See `skills/dynamo-maintainer/SKILL.md`: invariants, test tiers (unit, property,\nlive AWS), adding a feature end to end, release checklist, known traps. The\nwebsite (`../dynamo_website/AGENTS.md`) is regenerated from this repo with\n`./build-docs.sh`.","ref":"agents.html#maintaining-the-library-itself"},{"type":"extras","title":"Getting started","doc":"# Getting started\n\nA complete, minimal walkthrough: local DynamoDB, a repo, a schema, CRUD.","ref":"getting_started.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"1. Run DynamoDB Local - Getting started","doc":"```bash\ndocker run -p 8000:8000 amazon/dynamodb-local\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#1-run-dynamodb-local"},{"type":"extras","title":"2. Add the dependency and a repo - Getting started","doc":"```elixir\n# mix.exs\n{:dynamo, github: \"bmalum/dynamo\"}\n\n# lib/my_app/dynamo.ex\ndefmodule MyApp.Dynamo do\n  use Dynamo.Repo, otp_app: :my_app\nend\n\n# config/dev.exs\nconfig :my_app, MyApp.Dynamo,\n  region: \"eu-central-1\",\n  endpoint: \"http://localhost:8000\",\n  access_key_id: \"local\",\n  secret_access_key: \"local\"\n\n# lib/my_app/application.ex\nchildren = [MyApp.Dynamo]\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#2-add-the-dependency-and-a-repo"},{"type":"extras","title":"3. Define a schema - Getting started","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.Note do\n  use Dynamo.Schema\n\n  item do\n    table \"notes\"\n\n    field :owner, :string, partition_key: true\n    field :created_at, :utc_datetime, sort_key: true\n    field :title, :string\n    field :body, :string\n    field :tags, :string_set\n    field :pinned, :boolean, default: false\n  end\nend\n```\n\nKeys are generated for you: `pk = \"note# \"`, `sk = \" \"`.","ref":"getting_started.html#3-define-a-schema"},{"type":"extras","title":"4. Create the table from the schema - Getting started","doc":"```bash\nmix dynamo.create_table --schema MyApp.Note --repo MyApp.Dynamo\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#4-create-the-table-from-the-schema"},{"type":"extras","title":"5. Use it - Getting started","doc":"```elixir\nalias MyApp.{Dynamo, Note}\n\nnote = %Note{owner: \"alice\", created_at: DateTime.utc_now(), title: \"Hello\", tags: MapSet.new([\"intro\"])}\n\n{:ok, note} = Dynamo.put(note)\n\n{:ok, ^note} = Dynamo.get(%Note{owner: \"alice\", created_at: note.created_at})\n\n{:ok, nil} = Dynamo.update(note, pinned: true, tags: {:add, MapSet.new([\"important\"])})\n\n{:ok, page} = Dynamo.query(%Note{owner: \"alice\"}, descending: true, limit: 20)\nEnum.map(page.items, & &1.title)\n\n{:ok, nil} = Dynamo.delete(note)\n```\n\nEvery call returns `{:ok, _} | {:error, %Dynamo.Error{}}`; use the `!` variants\n(`put!`, `get!`, …) when you'd rather raise.","ref":"getting_started.html#5-use-it"},{"type":"extras","title":"6. Handle errors - Getting started","doc":"```elixir\ncase Dynamo.put(note, condition: \"attribute_not_exists(pk)\") do\n  {:ok, note} -> {:ok, note}\n  {:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :conditional_check_failed}} -> {:error, :already_exists}\n  {:error, %Dynamo.Error{} = e} -> raise e\nend\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#6-handle-errors"},{"type":"extras","title":"Next - Getting started","doc":"- [Data modelling](DATA_MODELLING.md) – composite keys, GSIs, single-table design\n- [Streaming & batches](STREAMING.md)\n- [Testing](TESTING.md)\n- [Agents.md](../Agents.md) – patterns and anti-patterns","ref":"getting_started.html#next"},{"type":"extras","title":"Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"# Data modelling with Dynamo","ref":"data_modelling.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Composite keys - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"Key fields are joined in declaration order with `key_separator` (default `#`).\nThe partition key is prefixed with the entity name so several entity types can\nshare a table.\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule Shop.Order do\n  use Dynamo.Schema\n\n  item do\n    table \"shop\"\n    entity_name \"order\"\n\n    field :tenant, :string\n    field :customer_id, :string\n    field :placed_at, :utc_datetime\n    field :order_id, :string\n    field :total, :decimal\n\n    partition_key [:tenant, :customer_id]\n    sort_key [:placed_at, :order_id]\n  end\nend\n\n{:ok, key} = Dynamo.Schema.primary_key(%Shop.Order{tenant: \"acme\", customer_id: \"c1\", placed_at: ~U[2024-01-15 10:00:00Z], order_id: \"o1\"})\nkey.pk  #=> %{\"S\" => \"order#acme#c1\"}\nkey.sk  #=> %{\"S\" => \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z#o1\"}\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- All partition key fields must be non-nil. `{:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :validation_error}}` otherwise.\n- Sort key fields may be partially populated (prefix). `%Shop.Order{tenant: \"acme\", customer_id: \"c1\", placed_at: dt}` gives `sk = \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\"`, which `query/2` turns into `begins_with`.\n- A value containing the separator is rejected. Keep `#` unless your data contains it.\n- `prefix_sort_key: true` renders `\"placed_at#2024-…#order_id#o1\"` if you want self-describing keys.","ref":"data_modelling.html#composite-keys"},{"type":"extras","title":"Sort key strategies - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"**Time ordering** – put an ISO 8601 datetime first; `descending: true` gives newest first.\n\n```elixir\nRepo.query(%Shop.Order{tenant: \"acme\", customer_id: \"c1\"}, sort_key: {:gte, \"2024-01-01\"}, descending: true)\n```\n\n**Type prefix in a single partition** – `sort_key [:kind, :id]` with `kind` as `\"PROFILE\"`, `\"ORDER\"`, `\"ADDRESS\"`:\n\n```elixir\nRepo.query(%Account.Item{account_id: \"a1\", kind: \"ORDER\"})           # begins_with \"ORDER\"\nRepo.query(%Account.Item{account_id: \"a1\"}, sort_key: {:eq, \"PROFILE\"})\n```\n\n**Range with BETWEEN** – composite string keys compare lexicographically, so an\nupper bound like `\"2024-01-31\"` excludes `\"2024-01-31T10:00:00Z#o1\"`. Append `~`\n(0x7E, above every character that can follow) to make the bound inclusive:\n\n```elixir\nRepo.query(%Shop.Order{...}, sort_key: {:between, \"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-31~\"})\n```","ref":"data_modelling.html#sort-key-strategies"},{"type":"extras","title":"Global secondary indexes - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\nitem do\n  table \"shop\"\n  field :order_id, :string, partition_key: true\n  field :status, :string\n  field :placed_at, :utc_datetime\n  field :total, :decimal\n\n  global_secondary_index \"StatusIndex\", partition_key: :status, sort_key: :placed_at\n  global_secondary_index \"TotalIndex\", partition_key: :status, sort_key: :total, projection: :keys_only\nend\n```\n\nGSI key attributes are the raw field values with their own types – no entity\nprefix, no separator. Numbers stay `N`, so range conditions work numerically:\n\n```elixir\nRepo.query(%Shop.Order{status: \"paid\"}, index: \"TotalIndex\", sort_key: {:gt, Decimal.new(\"100\")})\n```\n\n`mix dynamo.create_table --schema Shop.Order` creates the indexes with the right\nattribute types. Consistent reads are rejected on GSIs (DynamoDB does not support them).","ref":"data_modelling.html#global-secondary-indexes"},{"type":"extras","title":"Single-table design - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"Several schemas can point at the same table; the entity prefix keeps them apart:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule App.User do\n  use Dynamo.Schema\n  item do\n    table \"app\"\n    field :id, :string, partition_key: true\n    field :email, :string\n  end\nend\n\ndefmodule App.Session do\n  use Dynamo.Schema\n  item do\n    table \"app\"\n    field :user_id, :string, partition_key: true      # pk = \"session# \"\n    field :token, :string, sort_key: true\n    field :expires_at, :utc_datetime\n  end\nend\n```\n\nTo store child items *under the parent's partition* (adjacency list), point the\nchild's `entity_name` at the parent module and put the type in the sort key:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule App.Order do\n  use Dynamo.Schema\n  item do\n    table \"app\"\n    entity_name App.User                                # pk = \"user# \" – inherited from App.User\n    field :id, :string, partition_key: true             # the parent's id\n    field :kind, :string, sort_key: true, default: \"order\"\n    field :order_id, :string, sort_key: true\n    field :total, :decimal\n  end\nend\n\nRepo.query(%App.Order{id: \"u1\"})                       # all orders of u1: begins_with(sk, \"order\")\nRepo.get(%App.User{id: \"u1\"})                          # the parent, with its own sort key\n```\n\n`entity_name App.User` is resolved at compile time, so renaming the parent\nmoves both entities together and a typo is a compile error. The string form\n(`entity_name \"user\"`) does the same thing without the compile-time link.\nGive the parent a fixed sort-key value too (e.g. `field :kind, default: \"profile\"`)\nso parent and children never collide in the sort-key space. If two kinds share\na prefix (`\"order\"`, `\"order_note\"`), query with an explicit\n`sort_key: {:begins_with, \"order#\"}`.","ref":"data_modelling.html#single-table-design"},{"type":"extras","title":"Existing tables - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"For a table you did not design around this layout:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule Legacy.Customer do\n  use Dynamo.Schema, raw_keys: true\n\n  item do\n    table \"Customers\"\n    field :CustomerId, :string, partition_key: true    # attribute names are used as-is\n    field :Version, :integer, sort_key: true\n    field :Name, :string\n  end\nend\n```\n\n`mix dynamo.generate_schema Customers` writes this for you after sampling the table.","ref":"data_modelling.html#existing-tables"},{"type":"extras","title":"Embedded schemas - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"Nested structures keep their types when you declare them as embedded schemas:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule Shop.Address do\n  use Dynamo.Schema, embedded: true       # no table, keys or indexes\n\n  item do\n    field :street, :string\n    field :city, :string\n    field :geo, {:list, :float}\n  end\nend\n\ndefmodule Shop.Customer do\n  use Dynamo.Schema\n  item do\n    table \"shop\"\n    field :id, :string, partition_key: true\n    field :billing, Shop.Address\n    field :shipping, {:list, Shop.Address}, default: []\n    field :prices, {:list, :decimal}\n  end\nend\n```\n\nA `:map` field would hand you string-keyed maps with floats and strings back;\nan embedded schema gives you `%Shop.Address{}` with `Decimal`/`Date` values\nintact. Any table schema can be embedded as well – only its declared fields\nare stored, never the generated `pk`/`sk`.","ref":"data_modelling.html#embedded-schemas"},{"type":"extras","title":"Conditions without placeholders - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"Every `condition:`/`filter:` accepts a small DSL instead of a raw expression:\n\n```elixir\nRepo.put(order, condition: [pk: :not_exists])\nRepo.update(acct, [balance: {:decrement, 50}], condition: [balance: {:gte, 50}])\nRepo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u\"}, filter: {:and, [status: {:in, [\"open\", \"paid\"]}], {:not, [flagged: true]}})\nRepo.scan(Customer, filter: [{[:billing, :city], \"Berlin\"}, tags: {:contains, \"vip\"}])\n```\n\nValues are dumped with the field's type; placeholders (`#c0`, `:c0`) are\ngenerated so reserved words and odd attribute names are never a problem.","ref":"data_modelling.html#conditions-without-placeholders"},{"type":"extras","title":"Nil, defaults and removal - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"Nil fields are omitted from written items. Reading an item that lacks an\nattribute yields the struct default. To delete an attribute use\n`Repo.update(item, field: :remove)`; `Repo.update(item, field: nil)` stores an\nexplicit `NULL`, which loads back as `nil` too but is visible to\n`attribute_exists`.","ref":"data_modelling.html#nil-defaults-and-removal"},{"type":"extras","title":"Vector search - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"Store embeddings next to the data they describe and search them without a\nsecond database:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule Kb.Chunk do\n  use Dynamo.Schema\n\n  item do\n    table \"kb\"\n    field :doc_id, :string, partition_key: true\n    field :chunk_id, :string, sort_key: true\n    field :tenant, :string\n    field :lang, :string\n    field :text, :string\n    field :embedding, {:vector, 1024}\n\n    vector_index \"Semantic\",\n      field: :embedding,\n      distance: :cosine,\n      projection: :include,\n      projected_attributes: [:text, :lang],\n      partition_key: :tenant,\n      filters: [:lang]\n  end\nend\n\nembedding = MyApp.Embeddings.embed(\"how do I rotate credentials?\")   # your model, e.g. Bedrock Titan\n\n{:ok, %{results: hits}} =\n  Repo.search_vectors(Kb.Chunk, \"Semantic\", embedding, top_k: 8, filter: [tenant: \"acme\", lang: \"en\"])\n```\n\nDecisions:\n\n- **Dimensions** must equal your embedding model's output; `{:vector, n}` checks\n  it on write. Fewer dimensions cost less to store and search.\n- **Distance**: `:cosine` for raw embeddings, `:dot_product` if you normalise to\n  unit vectors (same ranking, cheaper), `:euclidean` when magnitude matters.\n- **Partition key** on the index (`partition_key: :tenant`) scopes each search\n  to one value and raises throughput quotas per value. It becomes mandatory in\n  `filter:`. Inline `filters:` narrow further with equality/range conditions.\n- **Projection** decides what a search returns and how much a write costs. The\n  vector itself is never returned unless you list it in `projection:`.\n- Vector indexes require on-demand billing, are eventually consistent, and are\n  immutable once created (add a new index instead).\n- The item is a normal item: `get`, `query`, `update` all work on it. Updating\n  the vector attribute re-indexes it.","ref":"data_modelling.html#vector-search"},{"type":"extras","title":"Custom types - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule App.Type.Money do\n  use Dynamo.Type\n\n  def dump(%Money{amount: a, currency: c}), do: {:ok, %{\"S\" => \"#{c}:#{a}\"}}\n  def dump(_), do: :error\n\n  def load(%{\"S\" => s}) do\n    [c, a] = String.split(s, \":\")\n    {:ok, %Money{amount: Decimal.new(a), currency: c}}\n  end\n\n  def load(_), do: :error\nend\n\nfield :price, App.Type.Money\n```\n\nFor values nested inside `:map`/`:list`/`:any` fields, implement `Dynamo.Encodable`\ninstead (one-way: they load back as plain maps).","ref":"data_modelling.html#custom-types"},{"type":"extras","title":"Checklist - Data modelling with Dynamo","doc":"- [ ] List access patterns before choosing keys\n- [ ] Partition key has high cardinality (no dates, no statuses)\n- [ ] Sort key supports the range queries you listed\n- [ ] GSIs for remaining patterns; `:keys_only`/`:include` where possible\n- [ ] Items < 400 KB – reference S3 for blobs\n- [ ] TTL attribute (`:integer` epoch seconds) for ephemeral data\n- [ ] `entity_name` set explicitly (string) if the module might be renamed and data already exists","ref":"data_modelling.html#checklist"},{"type":"extras","title":"Streaming, batches and transactions","doc":"# Streaming, batches and transactions","ref":"streaming.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Pages - Streaming, batches and transactions","doc":"`query/2` and `scan/2` return one `%Dynamo.Page{}`:\n\n```elixir\n{:ok, page} = Repo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, limit: 100)\npage.items                # [%Order{}]\npage.last_evaluated_key   # nil when done\npage.count                # items in this page\nEnum.map(page, & &1.total) # Page is Enumerable\n\n{:ok, next} = Repo.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, limit: 100, start_key: page.last_evaluated_key)\n```","ref":"streaming.html#pages"},{"type":"extras","title":"Streams - Streaming, batches and transactions","doc":"`Repo.stream/2` is a lazy `Stream` over all pages. Pass a struct to query or a\nschema module to scan.\n\n```elixir\nRepo.stream(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, page_size: 200)\n|> Stream.filter(&(&1.status == \"open\"))\n|> Stream.map(&notify/1)\n|> Stream.run()\n\nRepo.stream(User)\n|> Stream.chunk_every(25)\n|> Enum.each(fn chunk -> Repo.batch_write!(Enum.map(chunk, &migrate/1)) end)\n```\n\nErrors inside a stream are raised as `%Dynamo.Error{}` – wrap in `try` or let\nthe calling process crash and be restarted.","ref":"streaming.html#streams"},{"type":"extras","title":"Parallel scan - Streaming, batches and transactions","doc":"`segments:` runs one task per segment under the repo's `Task.Supervisor`;\n`max_concurrency:` (default `segments`) bounds how many fetch at once. Items\narrive interleaved; each task only fetches its next page after the previous one\nwas consumed, so memory stays bounded by `segments × page_size`.\n\n```elixir\nRepo.stream(User, segments: 8, max_concurrency: 4, page_size: 500)\n|> Flow.from_enumerable(max_demand: 200)      # optional: Flow for CPU-heavy work\n|> Flow.map(&expensive/1)\n|> Enum.to_list()\n```\n\nStopping early (`Enum.take/2`, an exception) stops the segment tasks.\n\n### `query_all` / `scan_all`\n\nConvenience for small result sets. `:limit` bounds the total.\n\n```elixir\n{:ok, orders} = Repo.query_all(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, limit: 500)\n```","ref":"streaming.html#parallel-scan"},{"type":"extras","title":"Batches - Streaming, batches and transactions","doc":"```elixir\n# BatchWriteItem: put structs and {:delete, struct}; chunked into 25 per request.\n# UnprocessedItems are retried with backoff (:batch_retries, default 5).\n{:ok, %{unprocessed: []}} = Repo.batch_write(new_users ++ Enum.map(stale, &{:delete, &1}))\n\n# BatchGetItem: keys of one schema, chunked into 100; UnprocessedKeys retried.\n{:ok, %{items: users, unprocessed_keys: []}} = Repo.batch_get(keys, consistent: true)\n```\n\nAny non-retryable error (`:access_denied`, `:resource_not_found`, …) aborts the\nbatch and is returned. A non-empty `unprocessed`/`unprocessed_keys` after all\nretries means sustained throttling – back off at the application level.","ref":"streaming.html#batches"},{"type":"extras","title":"Transactions - Streaming, batches and transactions","doc":"```elixir\nRepo.transaction(\n  [\n    {:check, %Account{id: \"src\"}, \"#b >= :amt\", names: %{\"#b\" => \"balance\"}, values: %{amt: 100}},\n    {:update, %Account{id: \"src\"}, [balance: {:decrement, 100}]},\n    {:update, %Account{id: \"dst\"}, [balance: {:increment, 100}]},\n    {:put, %Transfer{id: \"t1\", amount: 100}, condition: \"attribute_not_exists(pk)\"}\n  ],\n  client_request_token: \"transfer-t1\"\n)\n```\n\nWait – DynamoDB rejects two operations on the *same item* in one transaction,\nand so does `Dynamo.Request.transact_write/2` (before sending). Fold the check\ninto the update's `condition:` instead:\n\n```elixir\n{:update, %Account{id: \"src\"}, [balance: {:decrement, 100}], condition: \"#b >= :amt\", names: %{\"#b\" => \"balance\"}, values: %{amt: 100}}\n```\n\nUse `client_request_token:` for idempotency when retrying after a timeout –\nDynamoDB de-duplicates for 10 minutes. This matters because the client itself\nretries transport timeouts: a plain `Repo.update(acct, balance: {:decrement, 50})`\nthat times out may be applied twice. Either put it in a transaction with a\ntoken, or add a version guard:\n\n```elixir\nRepo.update(acct, [balance: {:decrement, 50}, version: {:increment, 1}], condition: [version: acct.version])\n```\n\nOn failure:\n\n```elixir\n{:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :transaction_canceled, cancellation_reasons: reasons}}\n# reasons: one per operation, e.g. [%{code: \"None\"}, %{code: \"ConditionalCheckFailed\", message: \"...\"}]\n```","ref":"streaming.html#transactions"},{"type":"extras","title":"Cost reminder - Streaming, batches and transactions","doc":"Scans read every item in the table regardless of filters. Streaming bounds\n*memory*, not *read capacity*. Prefer queries; reserve scans for migrations and\nexports.","ref":"streaming.html#cost-reminder"},{"type":"extras","title":"Testing applications that use Dynamo","doc":"# Testing applications that use Dynamo","ref":"testing.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Unit-test request building without I/O - Testing applications that use Dynamo","doc":"`Dynamo.Request` is pure, so you can assert on exactly what would be sent:\n\n```elixir\ntest \"orders are queried newest first\" do\n  {:ok, {\"Query\", payload}} = Dynamo.Request.query(%Order{user_id: \"u1\"}, descending: true, limit: 10)\n  assert payload[\"ScanIndexForward\"] == false\n  assert payload[\"Limit\"] == 10\nend\n```\n\nSame for `Dynamo.Schema.dump/1`, `Dynamo.Schema.primary_key/1` and `Dynamo.Update.build/2`.","ref":"testing.html#unit-test-request-building-without-i-o"},{"type":"extras","title":"Stub the HTTP layer with `Req.Test` - Testing applications that use Dynamo","doc":"The repo accepts any `Req` option, including `plug:`. In `config/test.exs`:\n\n```elixir\nconfig :my_app, MyApp.Dynamo,\n  region: \"us-east-1\",\n  access_key_id: \"test\",\n  secret_access_key: \"test\",\n  req_options: [plug: {Req.Test, MyApp.Dynamo}]\n```\n\nThen in a test:\n\n```elixir\ntest \"get returns nil when the item is missing\" do\n  Req.Test.stub(MyApp.Dynamo, fn conn ->\n    Req.Test.json(conn, %{})\n  end)\n\n  assert {:ok, nil} = MyApp.Dynamo.get(%User{id: \"u1\", email: \"e\"})\nend\n\ntest \"throttling surfaces as a retryable error\" do\n  Req.Test.stub(MyApp.Dynamo, fn conn ->\n    conn\n    |> Plug.Conn.put_status(400)\n    |> Req.Test.json(%{\"__type\" => \"com.amazonaws.dynamodb.v20120810#ProvisionedThroughputExceededException\", \"message\" => \"slow down\"})\n  end)\n\n  assert {:error, %Dynamo.Error{type: :provisioned_throughput_exceeded, retryable?: true}} =\n           MyApp.Dynamo.put(user)\nend\n```\n\nUse real captured DynamoDB bodies in stubs – error `__type`s are namespaced and\nthe message key varies between `message` and `Message`. `Dynamo.Error.from_aws/2`\nhandles both, and your tests should exercise the real shape.","ref":"testing.html#stub-the-http-layer-with-req-test"},{"type":"extras","title":"Use an in-memory fake - Testing applications that use Dynamo","doc":"This repository ships `test/support/fake_dynamo.ex`, a small in-memory DynamoDB\nimplemented as a plug. It supports put/get/delete/update, query with sort-key\nconditions and pagination, scan with segments, batch write/get including\n`UnprocessedItems`, and transactions. Copy it into your project's\n`test/support/` and start your repo against it:\n\n```elixir\nsetup do\n  {:ok, agent} = FakeDynamo.start_link()\n  start_supervised!({MyApp.Dynamo, req_options: [plug: FakeDynamo.plug(agent)], access_key_id: \"t\", secret_access_key: \"t\", region: \"us-east-1\"})\n  %{agent: agent}\nend\n```","ref":"testing.html#use-an-in-memory-fake"},{"type":"extras","title":"The library's own live test - Testing applications that use Dynamo","doc":"`test/integration/live_test.exs` exercises every feature against a real\nendpoint, creating and deleting its own tables (`dynamo_livetest`,\n`dynamo_livetest_raw`):\n\n```bash\n# AWS (credentials from the default chain)\neval \"$(aws configure export-credentials --profile my-profile --format env)\"\nAWS_REGION=eu-central-1 mix test --include integration test/integration/live_test.exs\n\n# DynamoDB Local\nDYNAMO_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8000 mix test --include integration test/integration/live_test.exs\n```","ref":"testing.html#the-library-s-own-live-test"},{"type":"extras","title":"Integration tests against DynamoDB Local - Testing applications that use Dynamo","doc":"```elixir\n# config/test.exs\nconfig :my_app, MyApp.Dynamo, endpoint: System.get_env(\"DYNAMO_ENDPOINT\", \"http://localhost:8000\"), ...\n```\n\nTag them `@tag :integration` and exclude by default (`ExUnit.start(exclude: [:integration])`).\nCreate tables in `setup_all` with `mix dynamo.create_table --schema` or via\n`MyApp.Dynamo.request(\"CreateTable\", payload)`.","ref":"testing.html#integration-tests-against-dynamodb-local"},{"type":"extras","title":"Protocol consolidation - Testing applications that use Dynamo","doc":"Schemas defined inside test files implement `Dynamo.Encodable`. Elixir\nconsolidates protocols after compilation, so add to `mix.exs`:\n\n```elixir\nconsolidate_protocols: Mix.env() != :test\n```\n\nOtherwise test-only schemas cannot be nested inside `:map`/`:list`/`:any` fields\n(they still work as top-level items).","ref":"testing.html#protocol-consolidation"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.35.1"}}